  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 1: SoV wavefunction rule. <x_m|Psi_B>/<x0|Psi_B> = N_m prod_s M^(s)_m / (vacuum), M_(a|bc) = det2[v(theta - (1+a)h), v(theta - b h)]_rows . v_k(theta - c h), N_m state independent. All 225 states, three (rows, k) conventions. *)\n{tims[\"SoV overlaps with kets\"], ovlM} = AbsoluteTiming[vecB . Transpose[ketC]];\nratioM = Table[ovlM[[m, A]]/(x0C . ketC[[A]]), {m, nS}, {A, nS}];\nlabIdx[l_] := First[Flatten[Position[labRule, l]]];\nsiteIdx = Table[{labIdx[allLabs[[m, 1]]], labIdx[allLabs[[m, 2]]]}, {m, nS}];\n(* det2[v(m21), v(m1)] v_k(m22) on rows {a,b}: one value per state, site, label *)\nsiteMono[rows_, k_] := Table[Table[With[{m1 = l[[1]], m21 = l[[2]], m22 = l[[3]]}, (vm[A, s, m21][[rows[[1]]]] vm[A, s, m1][[rows[[2]]]] - vm[A, s, m21][[rows[[2]]]] vm[A, s, m1][[rows[[1]]]]) vm[A, s, m22][[k]]], {l, labRule}], {A, nS}, {s, nL}];\nwfTest[rows_, k_] := Module[{sm = siteMono[rows, k], pred, rr, mask, worst, nExcl, bestA, Nrow},\n  pred = Table[Product[sm[[A, s, siteIdx[[m, s]]]], {s, nL}], {m, nS}, {A, nS}];\n  pred = Table[pred[[m, A]]/pred[[vacIdx, A]], {m, nS}, {A, nS}];\n  rr = ratioM/pred;\n  bestA = Table[Ordering[Abs[pred[[m]]], -1][[1]], {m, nS}];\n  Nrow = Table[rr[[m, bestA[[m]]]], {m, nS}];\n  worst = Table[Max[Abs[rr[[m]]/Nrow[[m]] - 1]], {m, nS}];\n  {Max[worst], Min[Abs[pred]], Nrow}];\n{tims[\"wavefunction tests (3 conventions)\"], wfRes} = AbsoluteTiming[Table[wfTest @@ rk, {rk, {{{1, 2}, 1}, {{2, 3}, 3}, {{1, 3}, 2}}}]];\nchecks[\"wavefunction rule M_x (rows {1,2},k=1; {2,3},3; {1,3},2): max rel dev over 225 labels x 225 states\"] = wfRes[[All, 1]];\nNm = wfRes[[2, 3]];\nchecks[\"N_m the same for all three conventions (max rel diff)\"] = Max[Abs[wfRes[[1, 3]]/wfRes[[2, 3]] - 1], Abs[wfRes[[3, 3]]/wfRes[[2, 3]] - 1]];\nGrid[{{\"max rel dev of <x_m|Psi_B>/<x0|Psi_B> vs N_m prod M (rows12 k1, rows23 k3, rows13 k2)\", N[wfRes[[All, 1]], 3]}, {\"min |predicted ratio| (zero-division guard)\", N[wfRes[[All, 2]], 3]}, {\"N_m identical across conventions (max rel diff)\", N[checks[\"N_m the same for all three conventions (max rel diff)\"], 3]}, {\"N_m: min, max abs\", N[{Min[Abs[Nm]], Max[Abs[Nm]]}, 4]}, {\"time (s): overlaps, tests\", {tims[\"SoV overlaps with kets\"], tims[\"wavefunction tests (3 conventions)\"]}}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Task 0a results — setup regression (cells 2-7 above; two runs, `Λ` changed in cell 2)\n\n| check | [2,1,0] (dim 8, 64 states) | [3,1,0] (dim 15, 225 states) |\n|---|---|---|\n| quantum determinant t3 = chi3 nu1(x) nu2(x-h) nu3(x-2h), exact at x = 3/7 | True | True |\n| # eigenstates; largest weight sector; min eigenvalue gap in a sector | 64; 10; 3.2e-3 | 225; 18; 6.4e-3 |\n| max abs residual of t_a psi = lambda_a psi at x = 19/23 | < 1e-52 | < 1e-50 |\n| dual Q's found at deg q^j = mu_j - L lambda3 (null-space dim 1); dual Baxter residual (relative) | True; < 1e-49 | True; < 1e-47 |\n| companion kets: <x0C\\|ket> = diagonal-frame <x0\\|psi>, max rel dev | < 1e-54 | < 1e-49 |\n| B(u) eigensystem gap; all roots on the two ladders 3+3; rule set size = dim V, every site triple in it | 1.6e-5; True; 8, True | 4.8e-6; True; 15, True |\n| # distinct (site-1, site-2) label pairs (= dim V^2); vacuum pair present; x0 = e1 (x) e1 exact left eigenvector of B | 64; True; True | 225; True; True |\n| **label rule** (a\\|bc): lambda2 <= a <= lambda1, 0 <= c <= lambda2, c <= b <= a, roots theta_s + {-1-a,-b,-c} h | reproduced, both sites | reproduced, both sites |\n| **wavefunction monomial** <x_m\\|Psi>/<x0\\|Psi> = N_m prod_s M^(s)_m/M^(s)_vac, max rel dev over all labels x states, rows{1,2}/k=1, {2,3}/3, {1,3}/2 | < 1e-43 / 1e-46 / 1e-46 | < 1e-39 / 1e-43 / 1e-43 |\n| N_m identical across the three conventions | < 1e-46 | < 1e-43 |\n| times (s): cells 2-7 (setup + B + wavefunction test) | 1.8 | 13 |",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Site-1 regression (general notebook Task 2): site-1 covectors tensor e1 in the L=2 SoV basis. K^(c2)[nu, x] = coefficient (in normalised-wavefunction units c_m N_m) of e_nu tensor e1 on the SoV state with site-1 label x and site-2 label (lambda1|lambda1 c2) *)\n{tims[\"expansion of e_nu tensor e1\"], cS} = AbsoluteTiming[LinearSolve[Transpose[vecB], Transpose[Table[N[UnitVector[d2, (nu - 1) d1 + 1], prec], {nu, d1}]]]];\nchecks[\"expansion error of e_nu tensor e1 in the SoV basis (max)\"] = Max[Abs[Transpose[vecB] . cS - Transpose[Table[UnitVector[d2, (nu - 1) d1 + 1], {nu, d1}]]]];\nKfull = cS * Nm;  (* d2 x d1, rows = SoV state m *)\nscaleK = Max[Abs[Kfull]];\nsuppM = Select[Range[nS], Max[Abs[Kfull[[#]]]]/scaleK > 10^-30 &];\nsite2Labs = Union[allLabs[[suppM, 2]]];\ngrp[c2_] := {-1 - Λ[[1]], -Λ[[1]], -c2};\ngrpSet = Table[grp[c2], {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}];\nchecks[\"site-2 labels in the support = {(lambda1|lambda1 c2), c2 = 0..lambda2}?\"] = {Length[site2Labs], Sort[site2Labs] === Sort[grpSet], Complement[site2Labs, grpSet]};\n(* label pair -> state index; the K matrices per site-2 group (rationalised, with the rationalisation error) *)\nmOfPair = Association[Table[allLabs[[m]] -> m, {m, nS}]];\nratz[x_] := Rationalize[Chop[x, 10^-40], 10^-40];\nKg = Association[Table[c2 -> Table[ratz[Kfull[[mOfPair[{labRule[[x]], grp[c2]}], nu]]], {nu, d1}, {x, d1}], {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}]];\nratErr = Max[Table[Max[Abs[N[Kg[c2], prec] - Table[Kfull[[mOfPair[{labRule[[x]], grp[c2]}], nu]], {nu, d1}, {x, d1}]]], {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}]];\nchecks[\"K rationalisation error (max abs, prec 60 data)\"] = ratErr;\nchecks[\"ranks of K^(c2), c2 = 0..lambda2\"] = Table[MatrixRank[Kg[c2]], {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}];\nchecks[\"max denominator digits in K\"] = Max[Table[Max[IntegerLength /@ Flatten[Denominator[Kg[c2]]]], {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}]];\n(* lambda_2^(c2) = v_k(theta2 - c2 h)/v_k(theta2 - lambda2 h), k-independence: v(theta2 - c2 h) parallel to v(theta2 - lambda2 h) *)\nfacL[A_, c2_] := vm[A, 2, -c2][[3]]/vm[A, 2, -Λ[[2]]][[3]];\nchecks[\"v_k(theta2 - c2 h)/v_k(theta2 - lambda2 h) independent of k (max rel spread over states, c2)\"] = Max[Table[Max[Abs[vm[A, 2, -c2]/vm[A, 2, -Λ[[2]]]/facL[A, c2] - 1]], {A, nS}, {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}]];\nchecks[\"v(theta_s) parallel v(theta_s - h) on both sites (2x2 minors, max)\"] = Max[Table[Norm[Flatten[Minors[Transpose[{vm[A, s, 0], vm[A, s, -1]}], 2]]]/(Norm[vm[A, s, 0]] Norm[vm[A, s, -1]]), {A, nS}, {s, nL}]];\n(* the overlap identity for covectors cov tensor e1:  <cov tensor e1|Psi>/<x0|Psi> * M1_vac = sum_c2 lambda2^(c2) sum_x (cov.K^(c2))_x M1_x, rows {2,3}, k = 3 *)\nsm23 = siteMono[{2, 3}, 3];\nvacL = labIdx[vacTrip];\novlExact[cov_, A_] := (kron[cov, e1] . ketC[[A]])/(x0C . ketC[[A]]);\novlK[cov_, A_] := Sum[facL[A, c2] Sum[(cov . Kg[c2])[[x]] sm23[[A, 1, x]], {x, d1}], {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}];\nidDevK[cov_] := Max[Table[Abs[ovlExact[cov, A] sm23[[A, 1, vacL]] - ovlK[cov, A]], {A, nS}]]/Max[Table[Abs[ovlExact[cov, A] sm23[[A, 1, vacL]]], {A, nS}]];\ngaussCov[{al_, be_, ga_}] := e1 . nexp[al Ee[1, 2]] . nexp[be Ee[1, 3]] . nexp[ga Ee[2, 3]];\nSeedRandom[11]; covRnd = RandomInteger[{-9, 9}, d1];\nchecks[\"overlap identity via K: max rel dev (generic Gauss rotation, random covector, 3 GT basis covectors)\"] = {idDevK[Normal[gaussCov[{2/3, -3/7, 5/4}]]], idDevK[covRnd], Max[Table[idDevK[uv[nu]], {nu, {1, 2, d1}}]]};\nGrid[{{\"expansion error\", N[checks[\"expansion error of e_nu tensor e1 in the SoV basis (max)\"], 3]}, {\"# SoV states in the support; site-2 labels (count, = groups?, extra)\", checks[\"site-2 labels in the support = {(lambda1|lambda1 c2), c2 = 0..lambda2}?\"]}, {\"K rationalisation error; max denominator digits\", {N[ratErr, 3], checks[\"max denominator digits in K\"]}}, {\"ranks of K^(c2), c2 = 0..lambda2\", checks[\"ranks of K^(c2), c2 = 0..lambda2\"]}, {\"k-independence of lambda2^(c2); v(th) || v(th-h)\", N[{checks[\"v_k(theta2 - c2 h)/v_k(theta2 - lambda2 h) independent of k (max rel spread over states, c2)\"], checks[\"v(theta_s) parallel v(theta_s - h) on both sites (2x2 minors, max)\"]}, 3]}, {\"overlap identity (rotation, random, basis)\", N[checks[\"overlap identity via K: max rel dev (generic Gauss rotation, random covector, 3 GT basis covectors)\"], 3]}, {\"# support states total, times (s)\", {Length[suppM], tims[\"expansion of e_nu tensor e1\"]}}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Site-1 regression (general notebook Task 3): coefficient tensors C^(c2)_{(n n'), c} (rows = minors (n,n'), n<n', in colex order over the points m = -1-lambda1..0; columns c = 0..lambda2) and the automatic bracket count *)\nmnL = Flatten[Table[{mPts[[i]], mPts[[j]]}, {j, 2, pPts}, {i, 1, j - 1}], 1];\nnMin = Length[mnL];\nmnIdx[{n_, np_}] := First[Flatten[Position[mnL, {n, np}]]];\n(* tensorOf: phi = vector over site-1 labels (labRule order) -> nMin x (lambda2+1) matrix; label x = {n, n', -c} sits at slot ((n,n'), c) *)\ntensorOf[φ_] := Module[{CC = ConstantArray[0, {nMin, Λ[[2]] + 1}]}, Do[With[{l = labRule[[x]]}, CC[[mnIdx[{l[[1]], l[[2]]}], -l[[3]] + 1]] = φ[[x]]], {x, d1}]; CC];\n(* 2-form of a column vector as an antisymmetric pPts x pPts matrix, wedge of two vectors, Pfaffians, Schur-type decomposition into wedges *)\namat[A_] := Table[Which[i == j, 0, i < j, A[[mnIdx[{mPts[[i]], mPts[[j]]}]]], True, -A[[mnIdx[{mPts[[j]], mPts[[i]]}]]]], {i, pPts}, {j, pPts}];\nwedgeV[F_, G_] := Table[F[[mi]] G[[mj]] - F[[mj]] G[[mi]], {mj, 2, pPts}, {mi, 1, mj - 1}] // Flatten;\npfaff[M_] := Module[{n = Length[M]}, If[n == 0, 1, If[OddQ[n], 0, Expand[Sum[(-1)^j M[[1, j]] pfaff[With[{r = Complement[Range[n], {1, j}]}, M[[r, r]]]], {j, 2, n}]]]]];\npf4list[A_] := With[{M = amat[A]}, Table[pfaff[M[[s, s]]], {s, Subsets[Range[pPts], {4}]}]];\npf6list[A_] := With[{M = amat[A]}, Table[pfaff[M[[s, s]]], {s, Subsets[Range[pPts], {6}]}]];\ndecompForm[A_] := Module[{M = amat[A], res = {}, ij, F, G, fw},\n  While[Not[AllTrue[Flatten[M], # === 0 &]],\n   ij = First[Select[Tuples[Range[pPts], 2], #[[1]] < #[[2]] && M[[#[[1]], #[[2]]]] =!= 0 &]];\n   F = M[[All, ij[[1]]]]/M[[ij[[1]], ij[[2]]]]; G = M[[All, ij[[2]]]];\n   AppendTo[res, {F, G}];\n   M = M - Table[F[[i]] G[[j]] - F[[j]] G[[i]], {i, pPts}, {j, pPts}]];\n  res];\n(* tool checks: bracket identity Bk2[F,G] = sum_{n<n'} (F^G)_{nn'} minor(n,n') on the whole point set (symbolic), Pfaffian criteria *)\nqS[j_, m_] := qq[j, m];\nminSym[{n_, np_}] := qS[2, np] qS[3, n] - qS[3, np] qS[2, n];\nbrQ[j_, F_] := Sum[F[[i]] qS[j, mPts[[i]]], {i, pPts}];\nBk2[F_, G_] := brQ[3, F] brQ[2, G] - brQ[2, F] brQ[3, G];\nFs0 = Array[ff, pPts]; Gs0 = Array[gg, pPts];\nchecks[\"bracket identity Bk2[F,G] = sum (F^G)_{nn'} minor_{23}(n,n'), symbolic on all points\"] = Expand[Bk2[Fs0, Gs0] - Sum[wedgeV[Fs0, Gs0][[i]] minSym[mnL[[i]]], {i, nMin}]] === 0;\nSeedRandom[5];\nrF = RandomInteger[{-5, 5}, pPts]; rG = RandomInteger[{-5, 5}, pPts]; rF2 = RandomInteger[{-5, 5}, pPts]; rG2 = RandomInteger[{-5, 5}, pPts]; rF3 = RandomInteger[{-5, 5}, pPts]; rG3 = RandomInteger[{-5, 5}, pPts];\nchecks[\"Pfaffian tools: F^G has all 4x4 Pfaffians 0; F1^G1 + F2^G2 does not; its Pfaffian rank is 4 (rank of amat)\"] = {Union[pf4list[wedgeV[rF, rG]]] === {0}, Union[pf4list[wedgeV[rF, rG] + wedgeV[rF2, rG2]]] =!= {0}, MatrixRank[amat[wedgeV[rF, rG] + wedgeV[rF2, rG2]]]};\n(* 6x6 Pfaffians on a synthetic 6-point form: rank <= 4 form has Pf6 = 0, rank-6 form does not (tool test independent of the rep) *)\nw6[F_, G_] := Table[F[[i]] G[[j]] - F[[j]] G[[i]], {i, 6}, {j, 6}];\na4 = w6[RandomInteger[{-5, 5}, 6], RandomInteger[{-5, 5}, 6]] + w6[RandomInteger[{-5, 5}, 6], RandomInteger[{-5, 5}, 6]]; a6 = a4 + w6[RandomInteger[{-5, 5}, 6], RandomInteger[{-5, 5}, 6]];\nchecks[\"6x6 Pfaffian: rank-4 form 0, rank-6 form nonzero\"] = {pfaff[a4], pfaff[a6] =!= 0};\nchecks[\"decompForm reconstructs random rank-4 form\"] = (Total[wedgeV[#[[1]], #[[2]]] & /@ decompForm[wedgeV[rF, rG] + wedgeV[rF2, rG2]]] === wedgeV[rF, rG] + wedgeV[rF2, rG2]);\n(* tensors at a generic rational rotation and at a random covector; rank of every column's 2-form *)\ngen0 = {2/3, -3/7, 5/4};\ncovGen = Normal[gaussCov[gen0]];\ntensorsOf[cov_] := Association[Table[c2 -> tensorOf[cov . Kg[c2]], {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}]];\ntenGen = tensorsOf[covGen]; tenRnd = tensorsOf[covRnd];\ncolRank[T_, c_] := MatrixRank[amat[T[[All, c + 1]]]];\nrankTab[ten_] := Table[Table[colRank[ten[c2], c], {c, 0, Λ[[2]]}], {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}];\nrkGen = rankTab[tenGen]; rkRnd = rankTab[tenRnd];\nsupportTab = Table[Table[Union[Flatten[mnL[[Flatten[Position[tenGen[c2][[All, c + 1]], x_ /; x =!= 0, {1}, Heads -> False]]]]]], {c, 0, Λ[[2]]}], {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}];\nslotsTab = Table[Table[Count[tenGen[c2][[All, c + 1]], x_ /; x =!= 0], {c, 0, Λ[[2]]}], {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}];\nchecks[\"rank of each column 2-form, generic rotation, per group c2 (rows) and column c\"] = rkGen;\nchecks[\"rank of each column 2-form, random covector\"] = rkRnd;\nautoGen = Total[Flatten[rkGen]]/2; autoRnd = Total[Flatten[rkRnd]]/2;\nchecks[\"automatic bracket count (generic rotation, random covector)\"] = {autoGen, autoRnd};\nchecks[\"tensor identity: sum over groups lambda2^(c2) sum_{nn',c} C minor v_k(-c) = overlap * M1vac (generic rotation, 225 states, rows 23, k 3)\"] = Max[Table[Abs[ovlExact[covGen, A] sm23[[A, 1, vacL]] - Sum[facL[A, c2] Sum[tenGen[c2][[mi, c + 1]] (vm[A, 1, mnL[[mi, 2]]][[2]] vm[A, 1, mnL[[mi, 1]]][[3]] - vm[A, 1, mnL[[mi, 2]]][[3]] vm[A, 1, mnL[[mi, 1]]][[2]]) vm[A, 1, -c][[3]], {mi, nMin}, {c, 0, Λ[[2]]}], {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}]], {A, nS}]]/Max[Table[Abs[ovlExact[covGen, A] sm23[[A, 1, vacL]]], {A, nS}]];\nGrid[{{\"points (m), # minors, columns\", {mPts, nMin, Λ[[2]] + 1}}, {\"tool checks (bracket identity; Pfaffians; 6x6; decompForm)\", {checks[\"bracket identity Bk2[F,G] = sum (F^G)_{nn'} minor_{23}(n,n'), symbolic on all points\"], checks[\"Pfaffian tools: F^G has all 4x4 Pfaffians 0; F1^G1 + F2^G2 does not; its Pfaffian rank is 4 (rank of amat)\"], checks[\"6x6 Pfaffian: rank-4 form 0, rank-6 form nonzero\"], checks[\"decompForm reconstructs random rank-4 form\"]}}, {\"support points per (group c2, column c) at the generic rotation\", supportTab}, {\"populated slots per (c2, c), generic rotation\", slotsTab}, {\"column ranks, generic rotation (rows c2 = 0..lambda2, columns c = 0..lambda2)\", rkGen}, {\"column ranks, random covector\", rkRnd}, {\"automatic bracket count per group c2 (generic rotation)\", Total[#]/2 & /@ rkGen}, {\"automatic bracket count: generic rotation, random covector; dim V, |Lambda|\", {autoGen, autoRnd, d1, Total[Λ]}}, {\"tensor identity (225 states) rel dev\", N[checks[\"tensor identity: sum over groups lambda2^(c2) sum_{nn',c} C minor v_k(-c) = overlap * M1vac (generic rotation, 225 states, rows 23, k 3)\"], 3]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Site-1 regression, reduced counts: bracket count of the site-1 tensors at the generic rotation and at a point of the best site-1 locus (adjoint quadric 16 (beta + alpha gamma) = 43 alpha^2 at t = 62/35, point (4, 23, 5); [3,1,0]: b3 = alpha^2, point (-3, 3, -2)); the known values are 5 / 4, 7 / 5 and 11 / 9 ([3,2,0]: curve point (1, 559/280, 403/140)). *)\nsite1Best = Which[Λ === {2, 1, 0}, {4, 23, 5}, Λ === {3, 1, 0}, {-3, 3, -2}, True, {1, 559/280, 403/140}];\nsite1Counts = {Total[Flatten[rankTab[tensorsOf[Normal[gaussCov[gen0]]]]]]/2, Total[Flatten[rankTab[tensorsOf[Normal[gaussCov[site1Best]]]]]]/2};\nGrid[{{\"site-1 bracket counts: generic rotation, best-locus point \" <> ToString[site1Best], site1Counts}, {\"expected (HANDOFF, general notebook)\", Which[Λ === {2, 1, 0}, {5, 4}, Λ === {3, 1, 0}, {7, 5}, True, {11, 9}]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Site-1 regression (cells 9-11; the machinery of `L2-site1-rotation-brackets-general.wb` cells 13 and 16, plus the reduced count)\n\n| check | [2,1,0] | [3,1,0] |\n|---|---|---|\n| support of e_nu (x) e1: # SoV states; site-2 labels = {(lambda1\\|lambda1 c2)}? | 12; True | 24; True |\n| ranks of K^(c2); rationalisation error; max denominator digits | 4, 8; 1.4e-90; 4 | 9, 15; 5e-88; 5 |\n| overlap identity via K (generic rotation / random covector / GT basis), rel dev | < 1e-45 / 1e-48 / 1e-48 | < 1e-42 / 1e-47 / 1e-48 |\n| **site-1 automatic bracket count** (generic = random covector) | **5** | **7** |\n| site-1 count at the best-locus point (adjoint quadric (4,23,5); [3,1,0]: b3 = alpha^2, point (-3,3,-2)) | **4** | **5** |\n| tool checks (bracket identity, Pfaffians, 6x6, decompForm) | True | True |\n\nThese are the site-1 numbers (5/7 automatic, 4/5 reduced) against which the site-2 counts below are compared.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 0b: the companion-frame one-site vacuum is the Gauss rotation with alpha = 1/w1, beta = -1/(w1 w2), gamma = (w1+w2)/(w1 w2); hence beta + alpha gamma = alpha^2 (first row of the 3x3 unipotent = (1, alpha, alpha^2)). Everything exact: dense MatrixExp of the rep generators at rational w. *)\nPppW[y_] := MatrixExp[(1/y[[1]]) Normal[Ee[1, 2]]] . MatrixExp[-(1/(y[[1]] y[[2]])) Normal[Ee[1, 3]]] . MatrixExp[((y[[1]] + y[[2]])/(y[[1]] y[[2]])) Normal[Ee[2, 3]]];\nΩc[y_] := e1 . PppW[y];\ngaussParOf[w_] := {1/w[[1]], -1/(w[[1]] w[[2]]), (w[[1]] + w[[2]])/(w[[1]] w[[2]])};\nwPts = {{2/3, -5/7}, {-3/2, 4/5}, {5/3, 7/2}};\nchkOmega = Table[Union[Flatten[Ωc[w] - Normal[gaussCov[gaussParOf[w]]]]] === {0}, {w, wPts}];\n(* 3x3 level: first row of exp(E12/w1) exp(-E13/(w1 w2)) exp((w1+w2)/(w1 w2) E23) in the defining rep *)\nee3b[i_, j_] := Table[KroneckerDelta[i, ii] KroneckerDelta[j, jj], {ii, 3}, {jj, 3}];\nPp3[w1_, w2_] := MatrixExp[ee3b[1, 2]/w1] . MatrixExp[-ee3b[1, 3]/(w1 w2)] . MatrixExp[((w1 + w2)/(w1 w2)) ee3b[2, 3]];\nfirstRowOK = Simplify[Pp3[ww1, ww2][[1]] - {1, 1/ww1, 1/ww1^2}] === {0, 0, 0};\nbetaAlphaGamma = Simplify[(gaussParOf[{ww1, ww2}][[2]] + gaussParOf[{ww1, ww2}][[1]] gaussParOf[{ww1, ww2}][[3]]) - gaussParOf[{ww1, ww2}][[1]]^2] === 0;\n(* converse: a rational point (alpha, gamma) with beta = alpha^2 - alpha gamma (the [3,1,0] best locus) equals Omega_c[{1/alpha, 1/(gamma - alpha)}] *)\nconvPts = {{-3, -2}, {-3, -1}, {-3, 1}, {-3, 2}, {5/2, -3/7}, {-4/3, 2/5}};\nchkConv = Table[Union[Flatten[Ωc[{1/p[[1]], 1/(p[[2]] - p[[1]])}] - Normal[gaussCov[{p[[1]], p[[1]]^2 - p[[1]] p[[2]], p[[2]]}]]]] === {0}, {p, convPts}];\n(* is Omega_c[w] (x) Omega_c[w] an exact left eigen-covector of t_a(u) with twist = companion matrix G(w1, w2, w3)? (any w3; control: transposed G) *)\nGc[{a_, b_, c_}] := {{a + b + c, -(a b + a c + b c), a b c}, {1, 0, 0}, {0, 1, 0}};\nOm2[w_] := kron[Normal[Ωc[w]], Normal[Ωc[w]]];\neigTest[w_, M_, a_, x_] := Module[{O2 = Om2[w], r, k}, r = O2 . tL2[a, x, M]; k = First[Ordering[Abs[O2], -1]]; {r === (r[[k]]/O2[[k]]) O2, r[[k]]/O2[[k]]}];\n{tims[\"eigen-covector test\"], eigRes} = AbsoluteTiming[Table[{w3, uu, Table[eigTest[wPts[[1]], Gc[Append[wPts[[1]], w3]], a, uu][[1]], {a, 3}], Table[eigTest[wPts[[1]], Transpose[Gc[Append[wPts[[1]], w3]]], a, uu][[1]], {a, 3}]}, {w3, {3/2, -4, 7/3}}, {uu, {3/7, 19/23}}]];\neigAll = And @@ Flatten[eigRes[[All, All, 3]]];\neigCtl = Flatten[eigRes[[All, All, 4]]];\n(* the same at the second w point, w3 = 5/3, as an independent check; the eigenvalue of t_1 vs the vacuum value *)\neigRes2 = Table[eigTest[wPts[[2]], Gc[Append[wPts[[2]], 5/3]], a, 3/7], {a, 3}];\nGrid[{{\"Omega_c[w] == Gauss rotation (1/w1, -1/(w1 w2), (w1+w2)/(w1 w2)), exact, 3 rational w\", chkOmega}, {\"3x3 first row of the Gauss product = (1, 1/w1, 1/w1^2), symbolic\", firstRowOK}, {\"beta + alpha gamma - alpha^2 = 0 on it, symbolic\", betaAlphaGamma}, {\"converse: rational (alpha, gamma) on beta = alpha^2 - alpha gamma equals Omega_c[{1/alpha, 1/(gamma-alpha)}] exactly (6 points)\", chkConv}, {\"Omega_c[w] (x) Omega_c[w] is an exact left eigen-covector of t_a(u), a = 1,2,3, twist G(w1,w2,w3): w3 in {3/2,-4,7/3} x u in {3/7,19/23}\", eigAll}, {\"control: twist G^T: eigen-covector? (False expected for a = 1, 2)\", eigCtl}, {\"second w point, w3 = 5/3, u = 3/7\", eigRes2[[All, 1]]}, {\"time (s)\", tims[\"eigen-covector test\"]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 0c: the two [3,1,0] closed-form lambda2-group measures (general notebook cell 47: columns (0,1) and (0,0), lone points Q^3(theta1 - h) and Q^3(theta1)) rewritten with alpha = 1/w1 and s = gamma/alpha = 1 + w1/w2, then checked against the exact tensors of the rotation Omega_c[w] and on all 225 states. Only meaningful for [3,1,0] (on the adjoint the quadric is not the vacuum family). *)\nClearAll[uNode, uDer, Fw01, Gw01, Fw00, Gw00, omW, lam01w, lam00w, uVecW, wedgeM2, brN, bk2N, Fa01, Ga01, Fa00, Ga00, omA, lam01a, lam00a];\nbrN[A_, j_, F_] := Sum[F[[i]] vm[A, 1, mPts[[i]]][[j]], {i, pPts}];\nbk2N[A_, F_, G_] := brN[A, 3, F] brN[A, 2, G] - brN[A, 2, F] brN[A, 3, G];\nwedgeM2[F_, G_] := Table[F[[i]] G[[j]] - F[[j]] G[[i]], {i, pPts}, {j, pPts}];\nIf[Λ =!= {3, 1, 0}, Grid[{{\"Task 0c is for [3,1,0] only: skipped for Λ = \" <> ToString[Λ]}}],\n Module[{uX1 = thN[[1]], uX2 = thN[[2]], uH = hN, S3 = {-4, -3, -2}, S4 = {-4, -3, -2, -1}, tt = tPar, wTest, resAll, symForms, omCheck, wedgeChk, ovlDev, vecW},\n  uNode[m_] := uX1 + m uH;\n  uDer[S_][u_] := Sum[Product[u - uNode[m2], {m2, DeleteCases[S, mm]}], {mm, S}];\n  (* alpha-forms (general notebook, 6c-3) *)\n  Fa01[a_][u_] := uH^4 a^((u - uX1)/uH)/(uDer[S3][u] (u - uX1) (u - uX2 + uH));\n  Ga01[a_][u_] := uH^3 a^((u - uX1)/uH)/(uDer[S3][u] (u - uX2 + uH));\n  omA[a_, g_] := 3 (g/a - 1)/(3 g/a - 2);\n  Fa00[a_, g_][u_] := -uH^4 a^((u - uX1)/uH)/(uDer[S4][u] (u - uX2 + uH)) (1 + (omA[a, g] - 1) KroneckerDelta[u, uNode[-1]]);\n  Ga00[a_, g_][u_] := Fa00[a, g][u] (u - uX1)/uH;\n  lam01a[tv_] := 48 (tv - 3) (tv + 1)/tv;\n  lam00a[a_, g_, tv_] := -12 (tv - 3) (3 g/a - 2);\n  (* w-forms: alpha = 1/w1, gamma = 1/w1 + 1/w2, s = 1 + w1/w2 *)\n  Fw01[w1_][u_] := uH^4 w1^(-(u - uX1)/uH)/(uDer[S3][u] (u - uX1) (u - uX2 + uH));\n  Gw01[w1_][u_] := uH^3 w1^(-(u - uX1)/uH)/(uDer[S3][u] (u - uX2 + uH));\n  omW[w_] := 3 w[[1]]/(w[[2]] + 3 w[[1]]);\n  Fw00[w_][u_] := -uH^4 w[[1]]^(-(u - uX1)/uH)/(uDer[S4][u] (u - uX2 + uH)) (1 + (omW[w] - 1) KroneckerDelta[u, uNode[-1]]);\n  Gw00[w_][u_] := Fw00[w][u] (u - uX1)/uH;\n  lam01w[w1_] := lam01a[tt] w1^-8;\n  lam00w[w_] := -12 (tt - 3) (w[[2]] + 3 w[[1]])/w[[2]] w[[1]]^-9;\n  vecW[fun_, S_] := Table[If[MemberQ[S, m], fun[uNode[m]], 0], {m, mPts}];\n  (* the w-reading of the end-point factor omega(theta1 - h) *)\n  omCheck = Simplify[omA[1/ww1, 1/ww1 + 1/ww2] - omW[{ww1, ww2}]] === 0;\n  symForms = {Fw01[ww1][uu], Gw01[ww1][uu], lam01w[ww1], Fw00[{ww1, ww2}][uu] /. KroneckerDelta[__] -> 0, lam00w[{ww1, ww2}], omW[{ww1, ww2}]};\n  wTest = {{2/3, -5/7}, {-3/2, 4/5}};\n  resAll = Table[Module[{cov = Normal[Ωc[w]], ten, decs, lhs, rhsMode, devs, w1 = w[[1]]},\n     ten = tensorsOf[cov];\n     wedgeChk = {amat[ten[0][[All, 2]]] === lam01w[w1] wedgeM2[vecW[Fw01[w1], S3], vecW[Gw01[w1], S3]], amat[ten[0][[All, 1]]] === lam00w[w] wedgeM2[vecW[Fw00[w], S4], vecW[Gw00[w], S4]]};\n     decs = Flatten[Table[Map[{c2, c, #[[1]], #[[2]]} &, decompForm[ten[c2][[All, c + 1]]]], {c2, 0, Λ[[2]]}, {c, 0, Λ[[2]]}], 2];\n     lhs = Table[ovlExact[cov, A] sm23[[A, 1, vacL]], {A, nS}];\n     rhsMode[mode_] := Module[{dd = decs}, \n       dd = Which[mode == \"decomp\", dd, mode == \"01\", Append[DeleteCases[dd, {0, 1, __}], {0, 1, lam01w[w1] vecW[Fw01[w1], S3], vecW[Gw01[w1], S3]}],\n          mode == \"00\", Append[DeleteCases[dd, {0, 0, __}], {0, 0, lam00w[w] vecW[Fw00[w], S4], vecW[Gw00[w], S4]}],\n          True, Join[DeleteCases[dd, {0, 1, __} | {0, 0, __}], {{0, 1, lam01w[w1] vecW[Fw01[w1], S3], vecW[Gw01[w1], S3]}, {0, 0, lam00w[w] vecW[Fw00[w], S4], vecW[Gw00[w], S4]}}]];\n       Max[Abs[lhs - Table[Sum[facL[A, d[[1]]] bk2N[A, d[[3]], d[[4]]] vm[A, 1, -d[[2]]][[3]], {d, dd}], {A, nS}]]]/Max[Abs[lhs]]];\n     devs = rhsMode /@ {\"decomp\", \"01\", \"00\", \"both\"};\n     {w, wedgeChk, N[devs, 3], Length[decs]}], {w, wTest}];\n  Grid[{{\"alpha-form and w-form of the (0,1) measure: F(u) = h^4 alpha^((u-th1)/h)/(P3'(u)(u-th1)(u-th2+h)) -> F(u) = h^4 w1^(-(u-th1)/h)/(P3'(u)(u-th1)(u-th2+h)), G(u) = h^3 w1^(-(u-th1)/h)/(P3'(u)(u-th2+h)), amplitude lam01 alpha^8 = 48 (t-3)(t+1)/(t w1^8)\", {Fw01[ww1][uu], Gw01[ww1][uu], lam01w[ww1]}},\n    {\"(0,0): F(u) = -h^4 w1^(-(u-th1)/h) om(u)/(P4'(u)(u-th2+h)), G = F (u-th1)/h, amplitude lam00 alpha^9 = -12 (t-3)(w2+3 w1)/(w2 w1^9); om = 1 except om(th1-h) = 3 w1/(w2+3 w1)\", {lam00w[{ww1, ww2}], omW[{ww1, ww2}]}},\n    {\"w-reading of the exception: 3(s-1)/(3s-2) with s = 1 + w1/w2 equals 3 w1/(w2 + 3 w1) (symbolic)\", omCheck},\n    {\"rational w, rows: {w, exact wedge identities (0,1),(0,0) vs the tensors of Omega_c[w], 225-state deviations (all columns decomposed numerically / (0,1) w-form / (0,0) w-form / both w-forms), # wedges}\", resAll}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]]]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Task 0b/0c results — the vacuum-family identification (cells 13-14)\n\n**(b) Companion-frame one-site vacuum** (`Ωc[w]` = e1 exp(E12/w1) exp(-E13/(w1 w2)) exp((w1+w2)/(w1 w2) E23), dense exact `MatrixExp` of the rep generators), identical results for both reps:\n\n| check | result |\n|---|---|\n| `Ωc[w]` == `gaussCov[{1/w1, -1/(w1 w2), (w1+w2)/(w1 w2)}]` exactly, 3 rational w (2/3,-5/7), (-3/2,4/5), (5/3,7/2) | True, True, True |\n| 3x3 level: first row of exp(E12/w1) exp(-E13/(w1 w2)) exp((w1+w2)/(w1 w2) E23) = (1, 1/w1, 1/w1^2), symbolic | True |\n| beta + alpha gamma - alpha^2 = 0 on it (symbolic) | True: b3 = alpha^2 |\n| converse: rational (alpha, gamma) on beta = alpha^2 - alpha gamma ([3,1,0] best locus), 6 points (incl. the points (-3,3,-2), (-3,6,-1), (-3,12,1), (-3,15,2) of the site-1 table) equal `Ωc[{1/alpha, 1/(gamma-alpha)}]` exactly | True x 6 |\n| `Ωc[w]`(x)`Ωc[w]` is an EXACT left eigen-covector (r === lambda r0 on the sparse exact t_a) of the transfer matrices t_1, t_2, t_3 at u = 3/7 and 19/23 with the **companion-matrix twist G(w1,w2,w3) = [[chi1,-chi2,chi3],[1,0,0],[0,1,0]]**, for w3 = 3/2, -4, 7/3 (any w3) and a second w point (w3 = 5/3) | True (all a = 1,2,3) |\n| control: the transposed twist G^T | False for a = 1, 2 (True only for the scalar t_3) |\n\nSo `Ωc` really is the vacuum with bra twist w, and the [3,1,0] 5-bracket locus beta + alpha gamma = alpha^2 is exactly {Ωc[(w1,w2)] : w1 = 1/alpha, w2 = 1/(gamma - alpha)}. (On the adjoint the best site-1 locus has cc = (t-3)/(2(t-2)) != 1: the vacuum family there costs the generic 5 brackets.)\n\n**(c) The two [3,1,0] lambda2-group closed-form measures with alpha = 1/w1, s = gamma/alpha = 1 + w1/w2** (cell 14, [3,1,0] only; skipped on the adjoint). With P3'(u), P4'(u) the node polynomials' derivatives (supports {-4,-3,-2} resp. {-4,..,-1} of ladder 1):\n\n- column (0,1), lone Q^3(theta1 - h): F(u) = h^4 **w1^(-(u-theta1)/h)** / (P3'(u)(u-theta1)(u-theta2+h)), G(u) = h^3 w1^(-(u-theta1)/h)/(P3'(u)(u-theta2+h)), amplitude lam01 alpha^8 = 48 (t-3)(t+1)/(t w1^8) (= -100104/(1085 w1^8) at t = 62/35);\n- column (0,0), lone Q^3(theta1): F(u) = -h^4 w1^(-(u-theta1)/h) om(u)/(P4'(u)(u-theta2+h)), G = F (u-theta1)/h, amplitude lam00 alpha^9 = -12 (t-3)(w2+3 w1)/(w2 w1^9) (= 516 (3 w1 + w2)/(35 w1^9 w2) at t = 62/35); **om = 1 except om(theta1 - h) = 3 w1/(w2 + 3 w1)**.\n\nSo both read as (bra twist w1^(-(u-theta1)/h)) x (SoV measure of the support) x 1/(u-theta2+h) x (low-degree polynomial). **The exception has a clean w-reading**: omega(theta1-h) = 3(s-1)/(3s-2) = 3 w1/(w2 + 3 w1) (symbolic, True), i.e. 3/(3 + w2/w1): a ratio of the two vacuum twist parameters, no t-dependence.\n\nVerification at rational w = (2/3,-5/7) and (-3/2,4/5): exact wedge identities amat(column (0,1)) = lam01 F^G and amat(column (0,0)) = lam00 F^G against the tensors of `Ωc[w]`: True, True at both points. Full overlap identity on all 225 states (all columns decomposed numerically / (0,1) as w-form / (0,0) as w-form / both): < 1e-43.9, 1e-43.8, 1e-43.8, 1e-43.7 at w = (2/3,-5/7) and < 1e-46.6, 1e-46.4, 1e-46.4, 1e-46.3 at w = (-3/2,4/5); 5 wedges.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 1: the mirror. Phi = e1 (x) e_nu (site 1 = SoV vacuum covector e1, site 2 = GT covector e_nu): expansion in the L=2 SoV basis (LinearSolve against the transposed left eigenvectors of B), normalised-wavefunction units (times N_m). Support = which pairs (site-1 label x1, site-2 label x2) occur. Kh[x1] = (dim V x dim V) rational matrix (rows nu, columns site-2 label x2) of the SoV states with site-1 label x1. *)\n{tims[\"expansion of e1 (x) e_nu\"], cS2} = AbsoluteTiming[LinearSolve[Transpose[vecB], Transpose[Table[N[UnitVector[d2, nu], prec], {nu, d1}]]]];\nchecks[\"expansion error of e1 (x) e_nu in the SoV basis (max)\"] = Max[Abs[Transpose[vecB] . cS2 - Transpose[Table[UnitVector[d2, nu], {nu, d1}]]]];\nKfull2 = cS2*Nm; scale2 = Max[Abs[Kfull2]];\nrelSize = Table[Max[Abs[Kfull2[[m]]]]/scale2, {m, nS}];\nsupp2 = Select[Range[nS], relSize[[#]] > 10^-30 &];\nchecks[\"# SoV states in the support, smallest nonzero/largest (gap to the cut 1e-30)\"] = {Length[supp2], Min[Select[relSize, # > 10^-30 &]], Max[Select[relSize, # <= 10^-30 &]]};\nisSupp2[x1_, x2_] := MemberQ[supp2, mOfPair[{labRule[[x1]], labRule[[x2]]}]];\nsupMat = Table[If[isSupp2[x1, x2], 1, 0], {x1, d1}, {x2, d1}];\nlabName[l_] := \"(\" <> ToString[-1 - l[[1]]] <> \"|\" <> ToString[-l[[2]]] <> ToString[-l[[3]]] <> \")\";\ns1PerS2 = Table[{labName[labRule[[x2]]], Count[supMat[[All, x2]], 1], labName /@ labRule[[Flatten[Position[supMat[[All, x2]], 1]]]]}, {x2, d1}];\ns2PerS1 = Table[{labName[labRule[[x1]]], Count[supMat[[x1]], 1], labName /@ labRule[[Flatten[Position[supMat[[x1]], 1]]]]}, {x1, d1}];\nfamS1 = Table[grp[c1], {c1, 0, Λ[[2]]}];\ninFam = Count[Flatten[Table[If[supMat[[x1, x2]] == 1 && MemberQ[famS1, labRule[[x1]]], 1, 0], {x1, d1}, {x2, d1}]], 1];\nchecks[\"site-1 labels occurring in the support (count of d1), all of them (lambda1|lambda1 c1)?\"] = {Length[Union[allLabs[[supp2, 1]]]], Union[allLabs[[supp2, 1]]] === Sort[famS1], inFam, Length[supp2]};\n(* rationalised K per site-1 label *)\nKh = Association[Table[x1 -> Table[If[isSupp2[x1, x2], ratz[Kfull2[[mOfPair[{labRule[[x1]], labRule[[x2]]}], nu]]], 0], {nu, d1}, {x2, d1}], {x1, d1}]];\nratErr2 = Max[Table[Max[Abs[N[Kh[x1], prec] - Table[If[isSupp2[x1, x2], Kfull2[[mOfPair[{labRule[[x1]], labRule[[x2]]}], nu]], 0], {nu, d1}, {x2, d1}]]], {x1, d1}]];\nchecks[\"K rationalisation error (max abs); max denominator digits\"] = {ratErr2, Max[IntegerLength /@ Flatten[Denominator[Values[Kh]]]]};\nrkX1 = Table[MatrixRank[Kh[x1]], {x1, d1}];\nrkX2 = Table[MatrixRank[Table[Kh[x1][[All, x2]], {x1, d1}]], {x2, d1}];\nchecks[\"rank of K^(x1) (nu x x2), per site-1 label; rank per site-2 label (nu x x1)\"] = {rkX1, rkX2};\n(* the overlap identity via K: <e1 (x) cov|Psi>/<x0|Psi> M1_vac M2_vac = sum_{x1,x2} (cov.Kh[x1])_{x2} M1_{x1} M2_{x2}  (rows {2,3}, k = 3) *)\nsm23 = siteMono[{2, 3}, 3]; vacL = labIdx[vacTrip];\novlExact2[cov_, A_] := (kron[e1, cov] . ketC[[A]])/(x0C . ketC[[A]]);\novl2K[cov_, A_] := Sum[sm23[[A, 1, x1]]/sm23[[A, 1, vacL]] Sum[(cov . Kh[x1])[[x2]] sm23[[A, 2, x2]], {x2, d1}], {x1, d1}];\nidDev2[cov_] := Max[Table[Abs[ovlExact2[cov, A] sm23[[A, 2, vacL]] - ovl2K[cov, A]], {A, nS}]]/Max[Table[Abs[ovlExact2[cov, A] sm23[[A, 2, vacL]]], {A, nS}]];\nchecks[\"overlap identity via K (site 2): generic rotation / random covector / three GT basis covectors\"] = {idDev2[Normal[gaussCov[{2/3, -3/7, 5/4}]]], idDev2[covRnd], Max[Table[idDev2[uv[nu]], {nu, {1, 2, d1}}]]};\nGrid[{{\"expansion error\", N[checks[\"expansion error of e1 (x) e_nu in the SoV basis (max)\"], 3]}, {\"# SoV states in the support, {smallest kept, largest dropped} relative size\", {checks[\"# SoV states in the support, smallest nonzero/largest (gap to the cut 1e-30)\"][[1]], N[checks[\"# SoV states in the support, smallest nonzero/largest (gap to the cut 1e-30)\"][[2 ;; 3]], 3]}}, {\"site-1 labels in the support (# of dim V), all of the form (lambda1|lambda1 c1)?, # support states with such x1, total\", checks[\"site-1 labels occurring in the support (count of d1), all of them (lambda1|lambda1 c1)?\"]}, {\"site-1 labels per site-2 label: {x2, #, list of x1}\", s1PerS2}, {\"site-2 labels per site-1 label: {x1, #, list of x2}\", s2PerS1}, {\"K rationalisation error; max denominator digits\", {N[ratErr2, 3], checks[\"K rationalisation error (max abs); max denominator digits\"][[2]]}}, {\"ranks: K^(x1) per site-1 label (labRule order); per site-2 label\", {rkX1, rkX2}}, {\"overlap identity via K (rel dev): rotation (2/3,-3/7,5/4) / random covector / GT basis\", N[checks[\"overlap identity via K (site 2): generic rotation / random covector / three GT basis covectors\"], 3]}, {\"time (s)\", tims[\"expansion of e1 (x) e_nu\"]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 1b: the weight rule for the support. A label (a|bc) is a GT pattern ((lambda), (a, c), (b)); put wtOf(label) = (b, a + c - b, lambda1 + lambda2 - a - c). Test: the SoV covectors are weight-graded, i.e. <e1 (x) e_nu| has support only on pairs (x1, x2) with wtOf(x1) + wtOf(x2) = Lambda + wt(nu). Then compare the set of pairs allowed by this rule (some nu of the required weight exists) with the actual support. *)\nwtOf[l_] := With[{a = -1 - l[[1]], b = -l[[2]], c = -l[[3]]}, {b, a + c - b, Λ[[1]] + Λ[[2]] - a - c}];\nnuSupport[x1_, x2_] := With[{m = mOfPair[{labRule[[x1]], labRule[[x2]]}]}, Flatten[Position[Abs[Kfull2[[m]]]/scale2, x_ /; x > 10^-30, {1}, Heads -> False]]];\nviolations = Flatten[Table[If[isSupp2[x1, x2], Select[nuSupport[x1, x2], wtOf[labRule[[x1]]] + wtOf[labRule[[x2]]] =!= wtL1[[#]] + Λ &], {}], {x1, d1}, {x2, d1}], 2];\nallowed = Table[MemberQ[wtL1 + ConstantArray[Λ, d1], wtOf[labRule[[x1]]] + wtOf[labRule[[x2]]]], {x1, d1}, {x2, d1}];\nallowedCount = Count[Flatten[allowed], True];\nallowedAbsent = Flatten[Table[If[allowed[[x1, x2]] && Not[isSupp2[x1, x2]], {labName[labRule[[x1]]], labName[labRule[[x2]]]}, Nothing], {x1, d1}, {x2, d1}], 1];\nsuppNotAllowed = Flatten[Table[If[isSupp2[x1, x2] && Not[allowed[[x1, x2]]], {x1, x2}, Nothing], {x1, d1}, {x2, d1}], 1];\nGrid[{{\"# pairs (x1, x2) in the support; # allowed by the weight rule\", {Length[supp2], allowedCount}}, {\"weight-rule violations among the nonzero K entries (nu with wt(x1)+wt(x2) != Lambda+wt(nu))\", Length[violations]}, {\"support pairs NOT allowed by the rule\", Length[suppNotAllowed]}, {\"allowed pairs absent from the support: #, first 12\", {Length[allowedAbsent], Take[allowedAbsent, UpTo[12]]}}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Task 1 results — the mirror Φ = e1 (x) e_nu: the site-1 support is NOT (λ1|λ1 c1) (cells 16-17)\n\n**Surprise (structural): the construction is strongly site-asymmetric.** For Φ = e_nu (x) e1 (site-1 rotation) only the site-2 labels (λ1|λ1 c2) occur (12 resp. 24 SoV states). For **Φ = e1 (x) e_nu the expansion in the L=2 SoV basis involves ALL dim V site-1 labels and all site-2 labels, on a \"triangular\" set of pairs: 35 of 64 SoV states for [2,1,0], 103 of 225 for [3,1,0]**; only 15 resp. 29 of these have x1 in the family {(λ1|λ1 c1)} (the labels whose factor M^(1)_{x1}/M^(1)_vac is a single Q^3 ratio). So the \"vacuum on the other site + one Q-ratio\" structure holds for the site-1 rotation (with vacuum on site 2) but NOT for the site-2 rotation (with vacuum on site 1): the ladder-1 factor is now the full monomial minor_1(-1-a,-b) v_3(theta1 - c h) of every label.\n\n| check | [2,1,0] | [3,1,0] |\n|---|---|---|\n| expansion error of e1 (x) e_nu in the SoV basis (max abs); gap to the support cut 1e-30 | 4e-90; kept >= 1.3e-3, dropped <= 7.5e-92 | 6e-88; kept >= 9.2e-5, dropped <= 9.2e-89 |\n| # support SoV states (of dim V^2) | 35 (of 64) | 103 (of 225) |\n| distinct site-1 labels in the support; all of the form (λ1\\|λ1 c1)? ; # support states with such x1 | 8 (all); False; 15 | 15 (all); False; 29 |\n| # site-1 labels per site-2 label x2 (labRule order) | (1\\|00):1, (1\\|10):3, (1\\|11):4, (2\\|00):2, (2\\|10):5, (2\\|20):7, (2\\|11):5, (2\\|21)=vac: 8 | (1\\|00):1, (1\\|10):3, (1\\|11):4, (2\\|00):2, (2\\|10):5, (2\\|20):9, (2\\|11):5, (2\\|21):10, (3\\|00):2, (3\\|10):6, (3\\|20):11, (3\\|30):14, (3\\|11):5, (3\\|21):11, (3\\|31)=vac: 15 |\n| # site-2 labels per site-1 label x1 (labRule order) | 1, 3, 5, 2, 5, 7, 4, 8 | 1, 3, 5, 2, 5, 9, 6, 11, 2, 6, 11, 14, 4, 9, 15 |\n| rank of K^(x1) (nu x x2), per site-1 label (labRule order) | 1, 2, 4, 2, 4, 6, 4, 8 | 1, 2, 4, 2, 4, 6, 5, 9, 2, 5, 9, 12, 4, 9, 15 |\n| rank per site-2 label (nu x x1) | 1, 2, 3, 2, 4, 6, 4, 8 | 1, 2, 3, 2, 4, 6, 4, 8, 2, 5, 8, 12, 4, 9, 15 |\n| rationalisation error of K (max abs, prec-60 data); max denominator digits | 6e-78; 7 | 2.7e-76; 11 |\n| overlap identity via K: <e1 (x) cov\\|Psi>/<x0\\|Psi> M1_vac M2_vac = sum (cov.Kh[x1])_x2 M1_x1 M2_x2, rel dev: generic rotation / random covector / GT basis | < 1e-44 / 1e-46 / 1e-45 | < 1e-41 / 1e-45 / 1e-44 |\n| **z-independence**: Kh exactly equal (rational matrices) at z' = (3/2,5/4,3/7) and z'' = (2,5/4,2/3) | **True, True** (driver cell 33) | **True, True** (driver cell 33) |\n| time (s) | 0.2 | 3.3 |\n\nRaw tables: the full lists of site-1 labels per site-2 label are printed by cell 16 (for [2,1,0]: x2 = (1\\|00): {(2\\|21)}; (1\\|10): {(2\\|20),(2\\|11),(2\\|21)}; (1\\|11): {(1\\|11),(2\\|10),(2\\|20),(2\\|21)}; (2\\|00): {(2\\|20),(2\\|21)}; (2\\|10): {(1\\|11),(2\\|10),(2\\|20),(2\\|11),(2\\|21)}; (2\\|20): {(1\\|10),(1\\|11),(2\\|00),(2\\|10),(2\\|20),(2\\|11),(2\\|21)}; (2\\|11): {(1\\|10),(1\\|11),(2\\|10),(2\\|20),(2\\|21)}; (2\\|21): all 8). Pattern: the vacuum x2 pairs with every x1, the vacuum x1 with every x2, and the set shrinks monotonically towards the corner labels (1\\|00); the matrix of allowed pairs is almost symmetric in (x1,x2) but not exactly.\n\n**Weight rule (cell 17).** The SoV covectors are NOT total-weight eigencovectors: a naive rule wt(x1) + wt(x2) = Λ + wt(nu) with wt(a\\|bc) = (b, a+c-b, λ1+λ2-a-c) fails (11 / 51 violating nonzero K entries for [2,1,0] / [3,1,0]; 3 / 6 support pairs outside the rule, 1 / 3 allowed pairs absent), and a direct linear solve for any additive weight assignment f(x1) + g(x2) = Λ + wt(nu) is inconsistent (rank 29 vs 30 unknowns/augmented, all three components, [3,1,0]). I could not characterise the support rule more sharply within two attempts; the groups below are therefore the raw ones (per site-1 label).",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 2: ladder-2 column tensors per site-1 label, ranks and automatic counts, and the (c1, c') block form with ladder-1 minors absorbed into 2-forms (plan Stage B notation). Per site-1 label x1 and column c' (lone point Q^3(theta2 - c' h)) the tensor C^(x1)_{(n n'), c'} = (cov.Kh[x1]) at the slot of the label (-1-a, -b, -c'); a column 2-form of rank 2r needs r ladder-2 bracket determinants Bk2^(2)[F,G] = <Q^3 F>_2 <Q^2 G>_2 - <Q^2 F>_2 <Q^3 G>_2 with the SCALAR factor M1_{x1}/M1_vac of ladder 1. *)\nClearAll[phi2, tens2, blockOf, halfRk, blockCount, brN2, bk2N2, colRk2, rankTab2, supportTab2, f1fac];\nphi2[cov_] := Table[(cov . Kh[x1]), {x1, d1}];   (* d1 x d1: [[x1, x2]] *)\ntens2[cov_] := Association[Table[x1 -> tensorOf[cov . Kh[x1]], {x1, d1}]];\ncolRk2[T_, c_] := MatrixRank[amat[T[[All, c + 1]]]];\nrankTab2[ten_] := Table[Table[colRk2[ten[x1], c], {c, 0, Λ[[2]]}], {x1, d1}];\nsupportTab2[ten_] := Table[Table[Length[Union[Flatten[mnL[[Flatten[Position[ten[x1][[All, c + 1]], x_ /; x =!= 0, {1}, Heads -> False]]]]]]], {c, 0, Λ[[2]]}], {x1, d1}];\nbrN2[A_, j_, F_] := Sum[F[[i]] vm[A, 2, mPts[[i]]][[j]], {i, pPts}];\nbk2N2[A_, F_, G_] := brN2[A, 3, F] brN2[A, 2, G] - brN2[A, 2, F] brN2[A, 3, G];\nf1fac[A_, x1_] := sm23[[A, 1, x1]]/sm23[[A, 1, vacL]];\n(* bracket identity on ladder 2 with the actual dual Q's of a random state: Bk2[F,G] = sum_{n<n'} (F^G)_{nn'} minor_23(n,n') with minor(n,n') = Q^2(n') Q^3(n) - Q^3(n') Q^2(n) *)\nSeedRandom[7]; rF2 = RandomInteger[{-5, 5}, pPts]; rG2 = RandomInteger[{-5, 5}, pPts];\nbrIdent2 = Max[Table[Abs[bk2N2[A, rF2, rG2] - Sum[wedgeV[rF2, rG2][[i]] (vm[A, 2, mnL[[i, 2]]][[2]] vm[A, 2, mnL[[i, 1]]][[3]] - vm[A, 2, mnL[[i, 2]]][[3]] vm[A, 2, mnL[[i, 1]]][[2]]), {i, nMin}]], {A, nS}]]/Max[Abs[VT]];\n(* per-label ranks at the generic rotation gen0 and the random covector *)\ngen0 = {2/3, -3/7, 5/4}; covGen = Normal[gaussCov[gen0]];\ntg = tens2[covGen]; trn = tens2[covRnd];\nrkTabG = rankTab2[tg]; rkTabR = rankTab2[trn];\nsupTabG = supportTab2[tg];\ncntLabG = Total[Flatten[rkTabG]]/2; cntLabR = Total[Flatten[rkTabR]]/2;\n(* the block form: A^(c1,c')[(m m'), (n n')] = phi_{x1 x2} with x1 = (m, m'; -c1), x2 = (n, n'; -c') *)\nblockOf[ph_] := Association[Table[{c1, cp} -> Module[{M = ConstantArray[0, {nMin, nMin}]}, Do[With[{l1 = labRule[[x1]], l2 = labRule[[x2]]}, If[l1[[3]] == -c1 && l2[[3]] == -cp, M[[mnIdx[{l1[[1]], l1[[2]]}], mnIdx[{l2[[1]], l2[[2]]}]]] = ph[[x1, x2]]]], {x1, d1}, {x2, d1}]; M], {c1, 0, Λ[[2]]}, {cp, 0, Λ[[2]]}]];\nhalfRk[v_] := MatrixRank[amat[v]]/2;\n(* matrix-rank decomposition B = Bc . R (R = row-reduced basis): ladder-1 forms = columns of Bc, ladder-2 forms = rows of R; count = sum_k (rank/2)(rank/2); tried in both orientations, minimum kept *)\nblockCountOne[M_] := Module[{R = DeleteCases[RowReduce[M], {0 ..}], piv, Bc}, If[R === {}, Return[{0, 0, {}}]]; piv = Table[First[Flatten[Position[R[[k]], x_ /; x =!= 0, {1}, Heads -> False]]], {k, Length[R]}]; Bc = M[[All, piv]]; {Length[R], Sum[halfRk[Bc[[All, k]]] halfRk[R[[k]]], {k, Length[R]}], Table[{halfRk[Bc[[All, k]]], halfRk[R[[k]]]}, {k, Length[R]}]}];\nblockCount[M_] := With[{a = blockCountOne[M], b = blockCountOne[Transpose[M]]}, If[a[[2]] <= b[[2]], a, {b[[1]], b[[2]], Reverse /@ b[[3]]}]];\nbgG = blockOf[phi2[covGen]]; bgR = blockOf[phi2[covRnd]];\nblkG = Table[k -> blockCount[bgG[k]], {k, Keys[bgG]}]; blkR = Table[k -> blockCount[bgR[k]], {k, Keys[bgR]}];\n(* the overlap identity from the bracket forms (per-label wedges): sum_{x1} M1_{x1}/M1_vac sum_{c'} sum_wedges Bk2^(2)[F,G] Q^3_2(theta2 - c' h) = <Phi|Psi>/<x0|Psi> M2_vac *)\ndecsLab[ten_] := Flatten[Table[Map[{x1, c, #[[1]], #[[2]]} &, decompForm[ten[x1][[All, c + 1]]]], {x1, d1}, {c, 0, Λ[[2]]}], 2];\nrecOK[ten_, decs_] := AllTrue[Flatten[Table[Total[Join[{ConstantArray[0, nMin]}, wedgeV[#[[3]], #[[4]]] & /@ Select[decs, #[[1]] == x1 && #[[2]] == c &]]] === ten[x1][[All, c + 1]], {x1, d1}, {c, 0, Λ[[2]]}]], TrueQ];\nlabDev[cov_, ten_] := Module[{decs = decsLab[ten], lhs, rhs},\n  lhs = Table[ovlExact2[cov, A] sm23[[A, 2, vacL]], {A, nS}];\n  rhs = Table[Sum[f1fac[A, d[[1]]] bk2N2[A, d[[3]], d[[4]]] vm[A, 2, -d[[2]]][[3]], {d, decs}], {A, nS}];\n  {Length[decs], Max[Abs[lhs - rhs]]/Max[Abs[lhs]], recOK[ten, decs]}];\n{tims[\"identity: per-label brackets\"], devLabG} = AbsoluteTiming[labDev[covGen, tg]];\ndevLabR = labDev[covRnd, trn];\n(* the block form identity: sum_{c1, c'} Q^3_1(theta1 - c1 h) Q^3_2(theta2 - c' h) sum_k Bk2^(1)[u_k wedges] Bk2^(2)[w_k wedges] *)\nblockDev[cov_, bg_] := Module[{lhs, rhs, terms},\n  lhs = Table[ovlExact2[cov, A] sm23[[A, 2, vacL]] sm23[[A, 1, vacL]], {A, nS}];\n  terms = Flatten[Table[Module[{M = bg[{c1, cp}], R, piv, Bc}, R = DeleteCases[RowReduce[M], {0 ..}]; If[R === {}, {}, piv = Table[First[Flatten[Position[R[[k]], x_ /; x =!= 0, {1}, Heads -> False]]], {k, Length[R]}]; Bc = M[[All, piv]]; Flatten[Table[Flatten[Table[{c1, cp, u, w}, {u, decompForm[Bc[[All, k]]]}, {w, decompForm[R[[k]]]}], 1], {k, Length[R]}], 1]]], {c1, 0, Λ[[2]]}, {cp, 0, Λ[[2]]}], 2];\n  rhs = Table[Sum[vm[A, 1, -t[[1]]][[3]] vm[A, 2, -t[[2]]][[3]] (brN[A, 3, t[[3, 1]]] brN[A, 2, t[[3, 2]]] - brN[A, 2, t[[3, 1]]] brN[A, 3, t[[3, 2]]]) bk2N2[A, t[[4, 1]], t[[4, 2]]], {t, terms}], {A, nS}];\n  {Length[terms], Max[Abs[lhs - rhs]]/Max[Abs[lhs]]}];\n{tims[\"identity: block form\"], devBlkG} = AbsoluteTiming[blockDev[covGen, bgG]];\nGrid[{{\"ladder-2 bracket identity Bk2^(2)[F,G] = sum (F^G) minor_23 (random integer F, G, all states, relative to max|Q|)\", N[brIdent2, 3]}, {\"column ranks (rows x1 in labRule order, columns c' = 0..lambda2), generic rotation\", rkTabG}, {\"same, random covector\", rkTabR}, {\"support points per column (generic rotation)\", supTabG}, {\"AUTOMATIC per-label count (ladder-2 brackets, ladder-1 factor a scalar): generic rotation, random covector\", {cntLabG, cntLabR}}, {\"per-label identity: # wedges, rel dev over all states, exact reconstruction (generic rotation); random covector\", {devLabG[[1]], N[devLabG[[2]], 3], devLabG[[3]], devLabR[[1]], N[devLabR[[2]], 3], devLabR[[3]]}}, {\"block form (c1, c'): {matrix rank r, count sum_k (rk/2)(rk'/2), {(rk/2, rk'/2) per k}}, generic rotation\", blkG}, {\"block form totals: separable count sum r, product count; random covector sum r, product count\", {Total[blkG[[All, 2, 1]]], Total[blkG[[All, 2, 2]]], Total[blkR[[All, 2, 1]]], Total[blkR[[All, 2, 2]]]}}, {\"block-form identity (generic rotation): # products, rel dev over all states\", {devBlkG[[1]], N[devBlkG[[2]], 3]}}, {\"dim V, |Lambda|; site-1 numbers for comparison\", {d1, Total[Λ], \"5 / 7 / 11 automatic, 4 / 5 / 9 reduced for [2,1,0] / [3,1,0] / [3,2,0]\"}}, {\"times (s)\", {tims[\"identity: per-label brackets\"], tims[\"identity: block form\"]}}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Task 2 results — ladder-2 tensors and automatic counts (cell 19)\n\nTwo ways to count, both exact. **Per-label** (columns of tensors per site-1 label x1, c' = lone point Q^3(theta2 - c' h); the ladder-1 factor M^(1)_{x1}/M^(1)_vac is a SCALAR): a column 2-form of rank 2r needs r ladder-2 brackets Bk2^(2)[F,G]. **Block form** (plan section 1): blocks A^(c1,c')[(m m'),(n n')] = phi_{x1 x2} with x1 = (m,m';-c1), x2 = (n,n';-c'), decomposed as sum_k u_k (x) w_k (matrix-rank decomposition by row reduction, both orientations, minimum kept), u_k a ladder-1 2-form, w_k a ladder-2 2-form, count sum_k (rank u_k/2)(rank w_k/2) products of one ladder-1 and one ladder-2 bracket determinant.\n\n| quantity | [2,1,0] | [3,1,0] |\n|---|---|---|\n| ladder-2 bracket identity Bk2^(2)[F,G] = sum (F^G)_{nn'} minor_23(n,n') (random integer F,G, all states) | < 1e-47 | < 1e-47 |\n| column ranks per x1 (labRule order), columns c' = 0..λ2, generic rotation | {0,2} {2,2} {2,2} {2,2} {2,2} {4,2} {2,2} {4,2} | {0,2} {2,2} {2,2} {2,2} {2,2} {4,4} {2,2} {4,4} {2,2} {2,2} {4,4} {4,4} {2,2} {4,2} {4,4} |\n| same for a random covector | identical | identical |\n| support points per column (generic): max | 4 (no column with >= 6 points: rank <= 4 automatic) | 5 (same) |\n| # rank-4 columns (= non-automatic columns of Task 3) | 2: x1 = (2\\|20), c'=0 and x1 = vac (2\\|21), c'=0 | 11 |\n| **AUTOMATIC per-label count, generic rotation = random covector** | **17** | **40** |\n| (site-1 numbers for comparison, generic / reduced) | 5 / 4 | 7 / 5 |\n| block form: matrix ranks r(c1,c') (generic) | 3, 3, 3, 2 (sum 11) | 6, 6, 6, 4 (sum 22) |\n| block form: product count (generic); random covector | 15 (explicit decomposition: 16 products); 16 | 35 (explicit: 38 products); 35 |\n| per-label overlap identity <Phi\\|Psi>/<x0\\|Psi> M2_vac = sum_{x1} M1_{x1}/M1_vac sum_{c'} sum_wedges Bk2^(2)[F,G] Q^3(theta2 - c' h): # wedges; rel dev all states (generic / random covector); exact reconstruction | 17; < 1e-44 / 1e-46; True | 40; < 1e-41 / 1e-44; True |\n| block-form overlap identity (generic rotation): # products; rel dev | 16; < 1e-44 | 38; < 1e-40 |\n| times (s) | 0.1 + 0.15 | 0.7 + 1.2 |\n\n**Reading.** The site-2 counts are far above the site-1 ones (17 vs 5, 40 vs 7) and above dim V = 8 / 15 in the [3,1,0] case: the ladder-2 bracket formula for a site-2 rotation on the vacuum is NOT a few-bracket expression (per-label it needs one ladder-1 monomial per label x1 times its own ladder-2 brackets). It is, however, still \"set by ladder lengths and ranks\": the per-label count is sum over the 8 / 15 site-1 labels of (rank/2) with all column ranks <= 4, and the block-form separable ranks (11 / 22) are the sizes of the two-ladder tensor. Compared with the det6 Laplace count of the vacuum pair (20 products of 3x3 bracket determinants) the 35-38 products at [3,1,0] are of the same order.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 3a: loci in g2 (Gauss chart g = exp(gA E12) exp(gB E13) exp(gC E23); first row b = (1, gA, gB + gA gC)). Symbolic tensors per site-1 label x1 and column c' (polynomial in gA, gB, gC); per column the 4x4 Pfaffians (decomposable <=> all vanish), Factor, genuine part (saturation by gA gB gC), dimension, conic-type factors gB + gA gC = cc gA^2. *)\nClearAll[dimOf, satGen, dimGen, lociRow, colS2, supPts2, colPf2, conicOf2, ccGuess];\ngVars = {gA, gB, gC};\ngaussCovS = Expand /@ Normal[e1 . nexp[gA Ee[1, 2]] . nexp[gB Ee[1, 3]] . nexp[gC Ee[2, 3]]];\nchecks[\"symbolic Gauss covector at gen0 equals the numeric one\"] = (gaussCovS /. Thread[gVars -> gen0]) === covGen;\n{tims[\"symbolic tensors\"], tenS2} = AbsoluteTiming[Association[Table[x1 -> tensorOf[Expand /@ (gaussCovS . Kh[x1])], {x1, d1}]]];\ncolS2[x1_, c_] := tenS2[x1][[All, c + 1]];\nsupPts2[x1_, c_] := Union[Flatten[mnL[[Flatten[Position[colS2[x1, c], x_ /; x =!= 0, {1}, Heads -> False]]]]]];\ncolPf2[x1_, c_] := DeleteCases[Union[Factor /@ pf4list[colS2[x1, c]]], 0];\ndimOf[gens_List] := Module[{gb, best = 0, el, ok = True},\n  If[gens === {}, Return[3]];\n  gb = TimeConstrained[GroebnerBasis[gens, gVars], 120, $Failed];\n  If[gb === $Failed, Return[\"timeout\"]]; If[gb === {1}, Return[-1]];\n  Do[If[Length[S] > best, el = TimeConstrained[GroebnerBasis[gens, S, Complement[gVars, S]], 120, $Failed];\n     If[el === $Failed, ok = False, If[el === {} || el === {0}, best = Length[S]]]], {S, Reverse[Rest[Subsets[gVars]]]}];\n  If[ok, best, {\"at least\", best}]];\nsatGen[gens_List] := If[gens === {}, {}, TimeConstrained[GroebnerBasis[Append[gens, 1 - wSat gA gB gC], gVars, {wSat}], 120, $Failed]];\ndimGen[sat_] := If[sat === $Failed, \"timeout\", dimOf[sat]];\nlociRow[name_, gens_List] := Module[{sat = satGen[gens]}, {name, If[gens === {}, \"automatic\", gens], dimOf[gens], If[sat === $Failed, \"timeout\", If[sat === {1}, \"empty\", Factor /@ sat]], dimGen[sat]}];\ncolKeys = Flatten[Table[{x1, c}, {x1, d1}, {c, 0, Λ[[2]]}], 1];\n{tims[\"column Pfaffians\"], pfTab2} = AbsoluteTiming[Association[Table[k -> colPf2 @@ k, {k, colKeys}]]];\nnontriv2 = Select[colKeys, pfTab2[#] =!= {} &];\nchecks[\"columns with 6 or more support points (rank <= 4 loci needed)\"] = Select[colKeys, Length[supPts2 @@ #] >= 6 &];\n{tims[\"column loci\"], lociCol2} = AbsoluteTiming[Table[lociRow[{labName[labRule[[k[[1]]]]], k[[2]]}, pfTab2[k]], {k, nontriv2}]];\n(* the natural guess: conic-type factors gB + gA gC = cc gA^2 (b1 b3 = cc b2^2); the adjoint site-1 constant is cc(t) = (t-3)/(2(t-2)) *)\nccGuess[tv_] := (tv - 3)/(2 (tv - 2));\nconicOf2[f_] := Module[{p = Expand[f], k},\n  If[Exponent[p, gB] == 1 && Exponent[p, gC] == 1 && Exponent[p, gA] == 2 && FreeQ[Coefficient[p, gB, 1], gA | gB | gC], k = Coefficient[p, gB, 1]; With[{rem = Expand[p/k - (gB + gA gC)]}, If[FreeQ[rem, gB | gC] && Exponent[rem, gA] == 2 && Coefficient[rem, gA, 1] === 0 && Coefficient[rem, gA, 0] === 0, -Coefficient[rem, gA, 2], None]], None]];\nallFac2 = Flatten[Table[Map[{labName[labRule[[k[[1]]]]], k[[2]], #[[1]]} &, Flatten[FactorList[#][[2 ;;]] & /@ pfTab2[k], 1]], {k, nontriv2}], 1];\nfacDistinct = DeleteDuplicatesBy[Select[allFac2, Not[MatchQ[#[[3]], _?NumberQ | gA | gB | gC]] &], {#[[1]], #[[2]], Expand[#[[3]]]} &];\nconicTab2 = Select[Table[{f[[1]], f[[2]], f[[3]], conicOf2[f[[3]]]}, {f, facDistinct}], #[[4]] =!= None &];\nnonConic2 = Select[facDistinct, conicOf2[#[[3]]] === None &];\nGrid[{{\"columns with >= 6 support points (none = rank <= 4 automatic)\", checks[\"columns with 6 or more support points (rank <= 4 loci needed)\"]}, {\"non-automatic columns {site-1 label, c'}\", {#, pfTab2[#]} & /@ nontriv2 // Length}, {\"t = theta12/h, adjoint guess cc(t) = (t-3)/(2(t-2))\", {tPar, ccGuess[tPar]}}, {\"conic-type factors gB + gA gC = cc gA^2: {label, c', factor, cc}\", conicTab2}, {\"other irreducible non-monomial factors {label, c', factor}\", nonConic2}, {\"column loci: {name, generators, dim V(I), genuine part, dim genuine}\", lociCol2}, {\"times (s): tensors, Pfaffians, column loci\", {tims[\"symbolic tensors\"], tims[\"column Pfaffians\"], tims[\"column loci\"]}}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 3b: which sets of non-automatic columns (site-1 label x1, c') can be made decomposable together by a genuine rotation (alpha beta gamma != 0)? Subset scan (smallest first, supersets of empty sets pruned, time budget 600 s), components of the non-empty genuine loci, rational points, and the bracket counts there: per-label count (sum of column ranks/2) and block-form counts (sum of matrix ranks r; product count). Also counts at special points: vacuum family (b3 = alpha^2), the site-1 best locus constant, the adjoint-type quadric. *)\nClearAll[subsetGens2, ratPoints, splitLocus, rankMat2, labCountAt, blkCountAt];\nsubsetGens2[S_] := DeleteCases[Union[Flatten[pfTab2 /@ S, 1]], 0];\nscanT0 = AbsoluteTime[]; emptiesL = {}; nonEmptyL = {}; unresolvedL = {};\nDo[Do[\n   If[AbsoluteTime[] - scanT0 < 600 && Not[AnyTrue[emptiesL, SubsetQ[S, #] &]],\n    With[{sat = satGen[subsetGens2[S]]},\n     Which[sat === $Failed, AppendTo[unresolvedL, S], sat === {1}, AppendTo[emptiesL, S], True, AppendTo[nonEmptyL, {S, sat}]]]], {S, Subsets[nontriv2, {size}]}], {size, 1, Length[nontriv2]}];\ntims[\"subset scan\"] = AbsoluteTime[] - scanT0;\nmaximalNE = Select[nonEmptyL, Function[e, Not[AnyTrue[nonEmptyL, #[[1]] =!= e[[1]] && SubsetQ[#[[1]], e[[1]]] &]]]];\nratGrid = {1, 2, -1, 3, 1/2, -2, 3/2, 4, -3, 2/3, 5, -1/2};\nratPoints[sat_List, nWant_: 2] := Module[{pts = {}, fi, sol, pt},\n  Do[If[Length[pts] < nWant,\n    Do[sol = Quiet[Solve[And @@ ((# == 0) & /@ (sat /. {fs[[1]] -> a1v, fs[[2]] -> a2v})), fs[[3]]]];\n     If[ListQ[sol], Do[pt = gVars /. Join[{fs[[1]] -> a1v, fs[[2]] -> a2v}, s]; If[VectorQ[pt, Element[#, Rationals] && # =!= 0 &], pts = Union[pts, {pt}]], {s, sol}]], {a1v, ratGrid}, {a2v, ratGrid}]], {fs, {{gA, gC, gB}, {gA, gB, gC}, {gB, gC, gA}}}];\n  If[pts === {}, fi = TimeConstrained[FindInstance[And @@ ((# == 0) & /@ sat) && gA gB gC != 0, gVars, Rationals, nWant], 40, {}]; If[ListQ[fi] && fi =!= {}, pts = Union[gVars /. fi]]];\n  Take[SortBy[pts, LeafCount], UpTo[nWant]]];\nlabCountAt[pt_] := Total[Flatten[rankTab2[tens2[Normal[gaussCov[pt]]]]]]/2;\nblkCountAt[pt_] := Module[{bg = blockOf[phi2[Normal[gaussCov[pt]]]], bc}, bc = Table[blockCount[bg[k]], {k, Keys[bg]}]; {Total[bc[[All, 1]]], Total[bc[[All, 2]]]}];\nsplitLocus[sat_List] := Module[{g = If[Length[sat] == 1, sat[[1]], PolynomialGCD @@ sat], facs, rest, out},\n  facs = Select[FactorList[g][[All, 1]], Not[FreeQ[#, gA | gB | gC]] &];\n  rest = If[Length[sat] == 1, {}, Select[Together /@ (sat/g), # =!= 0 &]];\n  out = ({#} &) /@ facs;\n  If[rest =!= {} && GroebnerBasis[rest, gVars] =!= {1} && (Length[facs] == 0 || Length[sat] > 1), AppendTo[out, rest]];\n  If[out === {}, {sat}, out]];\nideSummary[ide_List] := If[StringLength[ToString[ide, InputForm]] < 350, Factor /@ ide, {\"ideal with\", Length[ide], \"generators, max total degree\", Max[Exponent[# /. {gA -> sS gA, gB -> sS gB, gC -> sS gC}, sS] & /@ ide], \"(not printed)\"}];\n(* components, up to 3 rational points each, counts there *)\n{tims[\"components: points and counts\"], compTab2} = AbsoluteTiming[Table[With[{comp = c, pts = ratPoints[c, 3]}, {comp, dimOf[comp], pts, labCountAt /@ pts, blkCountAt /@ pts}], {c, DeleteDuplicatesBy[Flatten[splitLocus /@ (maximalNE[[All, 2]]), 1], Expand[#] & /@ # &]}]];\n(* special points: vacuum family b3 = alpha^2 (alpha = 1/w1, gamma = 1/w1 + 1/w2) *)\nvacPts = Table[{1/w[[1]], -1/(w[[1]] w[[2]]), 1/w[[1]] + 1/w[[2]]}, {w, {{2/3, -5/7}, {-3/2, 4/5}, {5/3, 7/2}}}];\nccAdj = (tPar - 3)/(2 (tPar - 2));\nadjPts = Table[{pp[[1]], ccAdj pp[[1]]^2 - pp[[1]] pp[[2]], pp[[2]]}, {pp, {{4, 5}, {4, 3}, {-3, 2}}}];\ngenCounts = {labCountAt[gen0], blkCountAt[gen0]};\nvacCounts = Table[{labCountAt[p], blkCountAt[p]}, {p, vacPts}];\nadjCounts = Table[{labCountAt[p], blkCountAt[p]}, {p, adjPts}];\nGrid[{{\"generic rotation: per-label count, block {sum r, products}\", genCounts}, {\"vacuum-family points Omega_c[w] (b3 = alpha^2): per-label count, block\", vacCounts}, {\"adjoint-type quadric points b3 = (t-3)/(2(t-2)) alpha^2 (t = \" <> ToString[tPar] <> \"): per-label, block\", adjCounts}, {\"maximal column sets decomposable together by a genuine rotation {set of (x1 index, c'), genuine ideal (or its size)}\", {#[[1]], ideSummary[#[[2]]]} & /@ maximalNE}, {\"minimal empty column sets (count; the 12 smallest)\", {Length[emptiesL], Take[SortBy[emptiesL, Length], UpTo[12]]}}, {\"unresolved (timeout)\", unresolvedL}, {\"components {ideal, dim, rational points, per-label counts, block counts {sum r, products}}\", {ideSummary[#[[1]]], #[[2]], #[[3]], #[[4]], #[[5]]} & /@ compTab2}, {\"times (s): scan, components\", {tims[\"subset scan\"], tims[\"components: points and counts\"]}}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 3c: reach table at finite twist (exact, no untwisting), mirrored for a site-2 rotation. In the diagonal frame the covector is (e1 P^-1) (x) (e1 rho(g2) P^-1) with P^-1 = L0 D0 U0 and e1 rho(P^-1) = e1 rho(U0); since rho(U) (x) rho(U) fixes every highest-weight ket, <e1 rho(U0) (x) e1 rho(g2 L0 D0) rho(U0)|HW> = <e1 (x) e1 rho(g2 L0 D0)|HW>: the undone site-2 covector is e1 rho(g2 L0 D0), site 1 is e1 = the HW covector of the slice weights nu - Lambda (same bookkeeping as the site-1 case with the roles of the two sites exchanged). The undo identity is checked EXACTLY on the HW kets. *)\nClearAll[ee3, Ppp3, Pmp3, P3, P3inv, rhoLow, rhoUp, undone2, reachOf, famSummary];\nee3[i_, j_] := Table[KroneckerDelta[i, ii] KroneckerDelta[j, jj], {ii, 3}, {jj, 3}];\nzq = zN;\nPpp3 = MatrixExp[(1/zq[[1]]) ee3[1, 2]] . MatrixExp[-(1/(zq[[1]] zq[[2]])) ee3[1, 3]] . MatrixExp[((zq[[1]] + zq[[2]])/(zq[[1]] zq[[2]])) ee3[2, 3]];\nPmp3 = MatrixExp[rVec[zq][[1]] ee3[3, 2]] . MatrixExp[rVec[zq][[2]] ee3[3, 1]] . MatrixExp[rVec[zq][[3]] ee3[2, 1]];\nP3 = Pmp3 . DiagonalMatrix[sVec[zq]] . Ppp3; P3inv = Inverse[P3];\nMg = P3inv; l21 = Mg[[2, 1]]/Mg[[1, 1]]; Mg[[2]] = Mg[[2]] - l21 Mg[[1]]; l31 = Mg[[3, 1]]/Mg[[1, 1]]; Mg[[3]] = Mg[[3]] - l31 Mg[[1]]; l32 = Mg[[3, 2]]/Mg[[2, 2]]; Mg[[3]] = Mg[[3]] - l32 Mg[[2]];\nL0 = {{1, 0, 0}, {l21, 1, 0}, {l31, l32, 1}}; D0 = Diagonal[Mg]; U0 = Inverse[DiagonalMatrix[D0]] . Mg;\nrhoLow[L_] := nexp[L[[2, 1]] Ee[2, 1]] . nexp[L[[3, 1]] Ee[3, 1]] . nexp[L[[3, 2]] Ee[3, 2]];\nrhoUp[U_] := nexp[U[[1, 2]] Ee[1, 2]] . nexp[(U[[1, 3]] - U[[1, 2]] U[[2, 3]]) Ee[1, 3]] . nexp[U[[2, 3]] Ee[2, 3]];\nchecks[\"P^-1 = L0 D0 U0 (3x3, exact); rho(P^-1) = rho(L0) rho(D0) rho(U0) on V (exact); e1 rho(P^-1) = e1 rho(U0)\"] = {L0 . DiagonalMatrix[D0] . U0 === P3inv, zeroM[SparseArray[PphInv1] - rhoLow[L0] . ρdiag[D0] . rhoUp[U0]], e1 . PphInv1 == ρdiag[D0][[1, 1]] (e1 . rhoUp[U0])};\nundone2[pt_] := Normal[e1 . nexp[pt[[1]] Ee[1, 2]] . nexp[pt[[2]] Ee[1, 3]] . nexp[pt[[3]] Ee[2, 3]] . rhoLow[L0] . ρdiag[D0]];\n(* weights, HW states of Lambda x Lambda (kernel of E12tot, E23tot per weight sector), slice weights nu - Lambda *)\nwV = Union[wtL1]; multV = Association[Table[w -> Count[wtL1, w], {w, wV}]];\nE12t = E1[1, 2] + E2[1, 2]; E23t = E1[2, 3] + E2[2, 3];\nhwKer = Association[Table[With[{sec = Flatten[Position[wtBasis, mu]]}, mu -> (Normal[SparseArray[Thread[sec -> #], {d2}]] & /@ NullSpace[Join[Normal[E12t[[All, sec]]], Normal[E23t[[All, sec]]]]])], {mu, Union[wtBasis]}]];\nhwMult = Association[KeyValueMap[#1 -> Length[#2] &, hwKer]];\nhwNu = Select[hwMult, # > 0 &];\nslice = Association[KeyValueMap[#1 - Λ -> #2 &, hwNu]];\nchecks[\"# HW states, # irreps in Lambda x Lambda; every slice weight is a weight of V\"] = {Total[hwNu], Length[hwNu], SubsetQ[wV, Keys[slice]]};\n(* exact undo identity on the HW kets, at rational g2 *)\nundoCheck[pt_] := Module[{cov = Normal[gaussCov[pt]], phiD, phiU},\n  phiD = kron[e1 . PphInv1, cov . PphInv1]; phiU = kron[e1, undone2[pt]];\n  And @@ Flatten[Table[Table[phiD . h === ρdiag[D0][[1, 1]] phiU . h, {h, hwKer[mu]}], {mu, Keys[hwKer]}]]];\nundoRes = Table[undoCheck[p], {p, {{1, 2, 3}, {-3, 6, -1}, {2/3, -3/7, 5/4}}}];\n(* families: generic rotations, the site-2 best locus b3 = 0, each genuine component with rational points of Task 3b, the vacuum family and the adjoint-type quadric *)\ngenPts = {{1, 2, 3}, {1/2, 1/3, 2}, {2, -1, 1/2}, {-3/2, 2/5, 3}};\nb3zeroPts = {{1, -2, 2}, {2, -6, 3}, {-1, 2, 2}, {3/2, -3, 2}};\nfamilies = Join[{{\"generic rotation\", genPts}, {\"b3 = 0 (gB = -gA gC)\", b3zeroPts}, {\"vacuum family b3 = alpha^2\", vacPts}, {\"adjoint-type quadric b3 = (t-3)/(2(t-2)) alpha^2\", adjPts}}, Table[{\"locus \" <> ToString[ideSummary[c[[1]]], InputForm] <> \" (dim \" <> ToString[c[[2]]] <> \")\", c[[3]]}, {c, Select[compTab2, #[[3]] =!= {} && #[[1]] =!= {gB + gA gC} &]}]];\nreachOf[pts_] := Module[{us = undone2 /@ pts},\n  Table[With[{ix = Flatten[Position[wtL1, w]]}, {w, multV[w], If[KeyExistsQ[slice, w], slice[w], 0], MatrixRank[us[[All, ix]]]}], {w, wV}]];\n{tims[\"reach table\"], reachTab} = AbsoluteTiming[Association[Table[fam[[1]] -> reachOf[fam[[2]]], {fam, families}]]];\nfamSummary[name_] := Module[{rt = reachTab[name]}, {name, Length[Select[rt, #[[4]] > 0 &]], Length[wV], And @@ (#[[4]] >= #[[3]] & /@ rt), Select[rt, #[[2]] > 1 &][[All, {1, 2, 4}]]}];\nGrid[{{\"L0, D0, U0\", {L0, D0, U0}}, {\"checks: LDU, rho(P^-1), e1 rho(P^-1); HW counts\", {checks[\"P^-1 = L0 D0 U0 (3x3, exact); rho(P^-1) = rho(L0) rho(D0) rho(U0) on V (exact); e1 rho(P^-1) = e1 rho(U0)\"], checks[\"# HW states, # irreps in Lambda x Lambda; every slice weight is a weight of V\"]}}, {\"UNDO IDENTITY on all HW kets (exact), at g2 = (1,2,3), (-3,6,-1), (2/3,-3/7,5/4)\", undoRes}, {\"weights of V: {weight, multiplicity}\", {#, multV[#]} & /@ wV}, {\"slice weights nu - Lambda (required rank)\", Normal[slice]}, {\"family: {name, # weights reached, # weights of V, all slice weights reached with full rank?, {weight, mult, rank} on multi-dim weight spaces}\", Table[famSummary[fam[[1]]], {fam, families}]}, {\"time (s)\", tims[\"reach table\"]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Task 3 results — loci in g2, joint loci, best locus, reach (cells 21-23 and the driver, cells 32-33)\n\nGauss chart g2 = exp(gA E12) exp(gB E13) exp(gC E23), b = (1, gA, b3 = gB + gA gC); groups = site-1 labels x1 (labRule order, \"x1 index\"), columns c' = 0..λ2. All Gröbner solves < 1 s (scan 0.04 s / 40 s, no timeout).\n\n**[2,1,0]** — only two columns are not automatic (rank 4, 4 support points): \n- (x1 = (2|20), c' = 0): Pf = (53266675/4826142) gB^2 **(gB + gA gC)^2**: genuine part **b3 = 0** (dim 2);\n- (x1 = vacuum (2|21), c' = 0): Pf = (17284333/16623378) gB^2 (66 gA^2 - 97 (gB + gA gC)) at t = 62/35: genuine part the **conic b3 = cc gA^2 with cc = 66/97** (dim 2).\n- Joint: EMPTY for genuine rotations (b3 = 0 and b3 = (66/97) alpha^2 meet only at alpha = 0). \n- cc(t): the same conic at t = 29/15: cc = 59/88; fitted exactly over 15 (h, theta) points (cell 33): **cc(t) = (t+2)/(2(t+1))**, equal to the site-1 adjoint constant with the argument **t -> 1 - t**: cc2(t) = cc1(1-t), cc1(t') = (t'-3)/(2(t'-2)) (the only match among t' = t + k, k - t, k = -6..6; t -> -t, t -> t+-1, t -> 2-t do NOT match). The constant is NOT 1: the site-2 conic is not the vacuum family.\n- Counts (per-label / block {sum r, products}): generic **17** / {11, 15}; vacuum family b3 = alpha^2 (3 points Ωc[w]): **17** / {11, 15} (no reduction); adjoint-type quadric (cc1(t)): 17; **b3 = 0: 13** / {10, 12} (dim 2, first row (1, alpha, 0), g2 = exp(gamma E23) exp(alpha E12)); conic cc = 66/97: **16** / {11, 14}.\n- Reach at finite twist (cell 23; exact; L0 = {{1,0,0},{-23/12,1,0},{5/6,-2/3,1}}, D0 = diag(1,-1/4,35/72), U0 = {{1,1,1},{0,1,10/3},{0,0,1}}): generic / vacuum family / quadric / conic: all **7 of 7 weights, rank 2 on (1,1,1)**, all 5 slice weights reached; **b3 = 0: only 5 of 7 weights, rank 1 on (1,1,1): NOT CG-complete** (the cheap locus is the site-2 analogue of beta = 0 in the site-1 table). 6 HW states in 5 irreps. **UNDO IDENTITY, exact on all HW kets, at g2 = (1,2,3), (-3,6,-1), (2/3,-3/7,5/4): True, True, True** (rho(U) (x) rho(U) fixes HW kets, so the same argument as at site 1).\n- Best locus: cheapest overall b3 = 0 (13) but not CG-complete; cheapest CG-complete: the conic 66 alpha^2 = 97 b3 (16).\n\n**[3,1,0]** — 11 non-automatic columns (x1 index, c'): (6,0), (6,1), (8,0), (8,1), (11,0), (11,1), (12,0), (12,1), (14,0), (15,0), (15,1) (= x1 labels (2|20), (2|21), (3|20), (3|30), (3|21), (3|31)). Conic-type factors gB + gA gC = cc gA^2 at t = 62/35 (and 29/15): column (2|21) c'=0: 2273/1188 (2957/1652); (3|30) c'=0: -453483/96224 (-18914/957); vacuum (3|31) c'=0: 8852/9021, 33/31, 334/291 (874/957, 59/58, 37/33). All other factors are non-conic (b3 itself, and quadratic/quartic/sextic polynomials). **Exact t-laws** (15 (h,theta) points, validated, cell 33): (2|21): (2t^2+5t-4)/(2(t-1)(t+2)); (3|30): (t-1)(8t^2+13t-7)/(6(t-2) t (t+1)); (3|31): (t^2+3t+6)/(3t(t+1)), **(t+2)/(2t)**, **2(t+3)/(3(t+1))**. The vacuum-family constant 1 occurs nowhere; no match with cc1(t') at t' = t + k, k - t (k = -6..6).\n- Genuine part EMPTY for the single columns (12,0) = ((3|30), c'=0) and (15,0) = (vacuum, c'=0) (5-point columns, five Pfaffians), as for the vacuum group of the site-1 case; 57 minimal empty column sets in all.\n- Maximal column sets decomposable together by a genuine rotation: 25 sets: 24 pairs, each giving a **dim-1 curve** (rational points found by the grid search for 4 of them: {(8,0),(8,1)}, {(8,0),(11,1)}, {(8,0),(14,0)}, {(8,1),(14,0)}; absence of points elsewhere is not a proof), plus one 4-set, namely **{(6,0),(6,1),(8,0),(11,0)} with locus (gB + gA gC)^2 = 0, i.e. b3 = 0 (dim 2)**.\n- Counts (per-label / block): generic **40** / {22, 35}; vacuum family b3 = alpha^2 (3 points): **40** / {22, 35} (no reduction); adjoint-type quadric: 40; **b3 = 0: 28** / {15, 23}; dim-1 curves, e.g. {31347670012201 gB = 1966671546840 gC^2, 12726297427 gA = -720392508 gC}: **38** / {22, 33}.\n- Reach: generic / vacuum family / quadric / all four curves with points: **12 of 12 weights, rank 2 on (1,1,2), (1,2,1), (2,1,1)**, all 8 slice weights; **b3 = 0: 7 of 12 weights, ranks 0, 1, 1 on the three double weights: NOT complete**. 10 HW states in 8 irreps; **UNDO IDENTITY exact on all HW kets: True x 3**.\n- Best locus: cheapest b3 = 0 (28, incomplete); cheapest CG-complete a dim-1 curve (38, only 2 below the generic 40).\n\n**Key question answered.** The site-2 best locus is NOT the vacuum family beta + alpha gamma = alpha^2 (nor, for the adjoint, the site-1 quadric): on the vacuum family `Ωc[w]` the site-2 bracket count equals the generic one (17 / 40), so the covectors `Ωc[w]` do not lie on any reducing locus. The asymmetry changes the structure: the cheap locus is **cc = 0 (b3 = 0)**, which however loses CG-completeness; the CG-complete reducing loci have t-dependent constants, for the adjoint cc2(t) = cc1(1-t) = (t+2)/(2(t+1)), for [3,1,0] the rational functions above.\n\n**Persistence (driver, cell 32).** The support size (35 / 103), the generic / b3=0 / vacuum-family counts (17/13/17 and 40/28/40) are identical at all 11 resp. 15 sampled (h, theta) points (t = 62/35, 29/15, 19/14, 6/35, 16/15, 5/2, 7/3, 3/5, 10/7, 82/21, -2/21, [3,1,0] also -8/35, 76/35, 40/21, 104/35); the b3 = 0 locus and its counts are t-independent.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 4a: closed-form ladder-2 measures on the best (fewest-bracket) site-2 locus b3 = 0, i.e. gB = -gA gC (first row of g2 = (1, alpha, 0); 2-dimensional, t-independent constant cc = 0; NOT CG-complete, see Task 3c). Every nonzero column 2-form is decomposed EXACTLY and symbolically by Schur-complement steps (pivot (i,j), F = M[All,i]/M_ij, G = M[All,j], residual M - F^G, rank drops by 2), gauge F_i = 0, F_j = -1, G_j = 0. Pivot rule: admissible pivots are those whose M_ij is a monomial in gA, gC times a constant (poles only on the excluded set alpha gamma = 0); all admissible pivots are scanned, the cheapest decomposition (LeafCount) is kept. *)\nClearAll[cfStall, tog, colLocB, wedgeM3, zeroMat3, goodFacQ2, goodPivQ2, nzPairs2, wedgeStep2, decompAll2, decCost2, bestDec2, cfDec2];\ncfStall = False;\nlocB = gB -> -gA gC;\ntog[x_] := With[{r = TimeConstrained[Together[x], 120, $Failed]}, If[r === $Failed, cfStall = True; x, r]];\ncolLocB[x1_, c_] := Expand /@ (colS2[x1, c] /. locB);\nwedgeM3[F_, G_] := Table[F[[a]] G[[b]] - F[[b]] G[[a]], {a, pPts}, {b, pPts}];\nzeroMat3[M_] := AllTrue[Flatten[M], # === 0 &];\ngoodFacQ2[f_] := NumberQ[f] || AnyTrue[{gA, gC}, FreeQ[Cancel[f/#], gA | gC] &];\ngoodPivQ2[x_] := With[{xt = Together[x]}, AllTrue[Join[FactorList[Numerator[xt]], FactorList[Denominator[xt]]][[All, 1]], goodFacQ2]];\nnzPairs2[M_] := With[{nz = Select[Subsets[Range[pPts], {2}], M[[#[[1]], #[[2]]]] =!= 0 &]}, With[{gd = Select[nz, goodPivQ2[M[[#[[1]], #[[2]]]]] &]}, If[gd === {}, nz, gd]]];\nwedgeStep2[M_, p_] := Module[{Fv, Gv, Rm}, Fv = tog /@ (M[[All, p[[1]]]]/M[[p[[1]], p[[2]]]]); Gv = M[[All, p[[2]]]]; Rm = Map[tog, M - wedgeM3[Fv, Gv], {2}]; {Fv, Gv, Rm}];\ndecompAll2[M_] := If[zeroMat3[M], {{}}, Flatten[Table[With[{st = wedgeStep2[M, p]}, Map[Prepend[#, {p, st[[1]], st[[2]]}] &, decompAll2[st[[3]]]]], {p, nzPairs2[M]}], 1]];\ndecCost2[dec_] := LeafCount[Map[Factor, dec[[All, {2, 3}]], {3}]];\nbestDec2[M_] := Module[{all = decompAll2[M]}, Map[{#[[1]], Map[Factor, #[[2]]], Map[Factor, #[[3]]]} &, First[SortBy[all, {decCost2, Length}]]]];\nnzCols = Select[colKeys, Not[zeroMat3[amat[colLocB @@ #]]] &];\n{tims[\"closed-form decompositions\"], cfDec2} = AbsoluteTiming[Association[Table[k -> bestDec2[amat[colLocB @@ k]], {k, nzCols}]]];\ncfRank2 = Association[Table[k -> Length[cfDec2[k]], {k, nzCols}]];\ncfResid2 = Association[Table[k -> Count[Flatten[Map[tog, Total[Join[{ConstantArray[0, {pPts, pPts}]}, wedgeM3[#[[2]], #[[3]]] & /@ cfDec2[k]]] - amat[colLocB @@ k], {2}]], x_ /; x =!= 0], {k, nzCols}]];\nchecks[\"closed form on b3 = 0: exact symbolic residual (# nonzero entries), all columns\"] = Total[Values[cfResid2]];\nsuppOfV[v_] := mPts[[Flatten[Position[v, x_ /; x =!= 0, {1}, Heads -> False]]]];\ncfLine[k_] := {labName[labRule[[k[[1]]]]] <> \", c' = \" <> ToString[k[[2]]], Length[cfDec2[k]], Map[{#[[1]], suppOfV[#[[2]]], suppOfV[#[[3]]]} &, cfDec2[k]]};\nGrid[{{\"b3 = 0 columns decomposed (nonzero): #\", Length[nzCols]}, {\"total # wedges (= bracket determinants), per-label count on b3 = 0 (compare Task 3b)\", {Total[Values[cfRank2]], labCountAt[{1, -2, 2}]}}, {\"symbolic residual of sum of wedges - column (0 = exact), all columns\", checks[\"closed form on b3 = 0: exact symbolic residual (# nonzero entries), all columns\"]}, {\"stalled Together?\", cfStall}, {\"{label, c'; # wedges; per wedge {pivot, supp F, supp G}}\", cfLine /@ nzCols}, {\"CLOSED FORMS: {label, c-prime; wedges {F, G} over the points m = \" <> ToString[mPts] <> \" (overlap = sum over x1 of M1_x1/M1_vac, over c-prime of Q^3(theta2 - c-prime h), over wedges of Bk2^(2)[F,G])}\", Table[{labName[labRule[[k[[1]]]]], k[[2]], Map[{#[[2]], #[[3]]} &, cfDec2[k]]}, {k, nzCols}]}, {\"time (s)\", tims[\"closed-form decompositions\"]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 4b: verification of the closed forms on b3 = 0 and their structure. (i) the full overlap identity on ALL states with the closed-form wedges evaluated at fresh rational points (alpha, gamma) of the locus, summed over site-1 labels with the scalar ladder-1 factor M1_{x1}/M1_vac and over c' with the lone Q^3(theta2 - c' h); (ii) exponent law: with gC = sR gA every nonzero entry is gA^(m + m' + k) a_{mm'}(sR), a free of gA, one offset k per column, a polynomial in sR; (iii) supports and delta functions of the wedge vectors. *)\nClearAll[cfAt2, cfOverlapDev2, aEntry2, kOff, kernDeg];\ncfAt2[pt_] := Flatten[Table[Map[{k[[1]], k[[2]], #[[2]] /. pt, #[[3]] /. pt} &, cfDec2[k]], {k, nzCols}], 1];\ncfOverlapDev2[pt_] := Module[{a = gA /. pt, g = gC /. pt, cov, decs, lhs, rhs},\n  cov = Normal[gaussCov[{a, -a g, g}]];\n  decs = cfAt2[pt];\n  lhs = Table[ovlExact2[cov, A] sm23[[A, 2, vacL]], {A, nS}];\n  rhs = Table[Sum[f1fac[A, d[[1]]] bk2N2[A, d[[3]], d[[4]]] vm[A, 2, -d[[2]]][[3]], {d, decs}], {A, nS}];\n  {Length[decs], Max[Abs[lhs - rhs]]/Max[Abs[lhs]], Min[Abs[lhs]]/Max[Abs[lhs]]}];\nfreshB = {{gA -> 5/2, gC -> -3/7}, {gA -> -4/3, gC -> 2/5}, {gA -> 7/3, gC -> 11/4}};\n{tims[\"closed-form state check\"], devB} = AbsoluteTiming[Table[cfOverlapDev2[pt], {pt, freshB}]];\n(* exponent law *)\naEntry2[k_, i_, j_] := Together[amat[colLocB @@ k][[i, j]] /. gC -> sR gA];\nkOff[k_] := Union[Flatten[Table[With[{e = Factor[aEntry2[k, i, j]]}, If[e === 0, Nothing, Exponent[Numerator[e], gA, Min] - Exponent[Denominator[e], gA, Min] - mPts[[i]] - mPts[[j]]]], {i, pPts}, {j, i + 1, pPts}]]];\nkernDeg[k_] := Max[Flatten[Table[With[{e = Together[aEntry2[k, i, j]/gA^(mPts[[i]] + mPts[[j]] + First[kOff[k]])]}, If[e === 0, 0, Exponent[Numerator[e], sR]]], {i, pPts}, {j, i + 1, pPts}]]];\nkTab = Table[{labName[labRule[[k[[1]]]]], k[[2]], kOff[k], kernDeg[k], FreeQ[Table[Together[aEntry2[k, i, j]/gA^(mPts[[i]] + mPts[[j]] + First[kOff[k]])], {i, pPts}, {j, i + 1, pPts}], gA]}, {k, nzCols}];\nsupWedge = Table[{labName[labRule[[k[[1]]]]], k[[2]], Map[{Length[suppOfV[#[[2]]]], Length[suppOfV[#[[3]]]]} &, cfDec2[k]]}, {k, nzCols}];\nGrid[{{\"overlap identity on all states, closed forms at 3 fresh points (gA, gC) of b3 = 0: {# wedges, max rel dev, min |lhs|/max |lhs| (non-vacuity)}\", {Length[nzCols], N[devB, 3]}}, {\"exponent law: {label, c', offsets k (single value), max degree in sR, gA-free}\", kTab}, {\"wedge support sizes {|supp F|, |supp G|} per column\", supWedge}, {\"time (s)\", tims[\"closed-form state check\"]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 4c: u-structure of the b3 = 0 columns. A^(x1,c')_{mm'} = gA^(m + m' + k) a_{mm'}(sR, t) (cell above), so the plane P = Im A of a rank-2 column is D P0 with D = diag(gA^m), P0 gA-free. Natural vector classes on the ladder-2 points m = -1-lambda1..0 (mirror of the site-1 test, ladder roles exchanged: cross-ladder poles at theta1 - n h give the factors (t - n - m)): (a) wgt_S(m) p(m), S = support of the column, wgt_S = 1/prod_{m' in S, m' != m} (m' - m); (b) the global SoV measure 1/(prod_{n != -m} (-n-m) prod_n (t-n-m)); (c) p(m); (d) p(m)/prod_n (t - n - m); p a polynomial of degree <= d (d = 0, 1, 2); n = 0..lambda1. dim(P0 cap class) at sR = 3/7 and the actual t of this run; rank-4 columns (two wedges) are listed only. *)\nClearAll[kern2, pw2, w8m, crossM, clsVec, clsDims];\nkern2[k_] := Table[Which[i == j, 0, i < j, aEntry2[k, i, j]/gA^(mPts[[i]] + mPts[[j]] + First[kOff[k]]), True, -aEntry2[k, j, i]/gA^(mPts[[j]] + mPts[[i]] + First[kOff[k]])], {i, pPts}, {j, pPts}] /. sR -> 3/7;\npw2[m_, k_] := If[k == 0, 1, m^k];\nw8m[m_] := 1/(Product[-n - m, {n, DeleteCases[Range[0, Λ[[1]]], -m]}] Product[tPar - n - m, {n, 0, Λ[[1]]}]);\ncrossM[m_] := 1/Product[tPar - n - m, {n, 0, Λ[[1]]}];\nwgtS[S_, m_] := 1/Product[mm - m, {mm, DeleteCases[S, m]}];\nclsVec[cls_, d_, S_] := Table[Table[If[cls == \"a\" && Not[MemberQ[S, m]], 0, Switch[cls, \"a\", wgtS[S, m], \"b\", w8m[m], \"c\", 1, \"d\", crossM[m]] pw2[m, k]], {m, mPts}], {k, 0, d}];\nclsDims[k_] := Module[{A0 = kern2[k], rk, ns, S},\n  rk = MatrixRank[A0]; If[rk != 2, Return[{\"rank \" <> ToString[rk]}]];\n  ns = NullSpace[A0]; S = Union[mPts[[Flatten[Position[Total[Abs[A0], {2}], x_ /; x =!= 0, {1}, Heads -> False]]]]];\n  Table[Table[Length[NullSpace[ns . Transpose[clsVec[cls, d, S]]]], {d, 0, 2}], {cls, {\"a\", \"b\", \"c\", \"d\"}}]];\n{tims[\"class dimensions\"], clsTab} = AbsoluteTiming[Table[{labName[labRule[[k[[1]]]]], k[[2]], MatrixRank[kern2[k]], clsDims[k]}, {k, nzCols}]];\n(* natural (a)-class with d = 1 (an affine polynomial times the support weights): which rank-2 columns have a vector of it in P (dim >= 1)? the dimension count is trivial for |S| <= 3 (P has dim 2 on |S| points: generic intersection with a 2-dim class is 1 when |S| = 3) *)\nnatCols = Select[clsTab, Length[#[[4]]] == 4 && #[[4, 1, 2]] >= 1 &];\nGrid[{{\"{label, c', rank, dims P0 cap class: rows a, b, c, d; columns d = 0, 1, 2} at sR = 3/7, t = \" <> ToString[tPar], clsTab}, {\"columns with dim(P0 cap class (a), d = 1) >= 1\", {#[[1]], #[[2]]} & /@ natCols}, {\"time (s)\", tims[\"class dimensions\"]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 4d: columns with a 3-point support S and rank 2: P = {v supported on S, n.v = 0} with ONE annihilator n on S; P = wgt_S Pol_1/nu with nu(m) = n_m (the vector with sum x_m p(m) = 0 for deg p <= 1 on 3 points is wgt_S). The u-form question is whether n_m is a NICE function of m: the quadratic through (m, n_m), its roots, at two values of sR (s-independence) and their offsets against t. Site-1 analogue (cell 6c-3 of the site-1 notebook): n_m = -m (t + m + 1), roots 0 and -(t + 1). *)\nClearAll[annRoots, xx];\nannRoots[k_, sv_] := Module[{A0 = kern2[k] /. sR -> sv, S, ns, offIdx, onIdx, sol, nm, quad},\n  S = Union[mPts[[Flatten[Position[Total[Abs[A0], {2}], x_ /; x =!= 0, {1}, Heads -> False]]]]];\n  If[MatrixRank[A0] != 2 || Length[S] != 3, Return[None]];\n  ns = NullSpace[A0];\n  offIdx = Flatten[Position[mPts, x_ /; Not[MemberQ[S, x]], {1}, Heads -> False]]; onIdx = Flatten[Position[mPts, x_ /; MemberQ[S, x], {1}, Heads -> False]];\n  sol = NullSpace[Transpose[Table[ns[[i, offIdx]], {i, Length[ns]}]]];\n  If[Length[sol] != 1, Return[{\"annihilator on S not unique\", Length[sol]}]];\n  nm = (sol[[1]] . ns)[[onIdx]];\n  quad = Expand[InterpolatingPolynomial[Transpose[{S, nm}], xx]];\n  {S, nm/First[Select[nm, # =!= 0 &]], Sort[xx /. Solve[quad == 0, xx]]}];\nroots3 = Table[{labName[labRule[[k[[1]]]]], k[[2]], annRoots[k, 3/7], annRoots[k, 5/2]}, {k, nzCols}];\nroots3 = Select[roots3, #[[3]] =!= None &];\nGrid[{{\"3-point-support rank-2 columns: {label, c', {S, normalised n_m, roots of the quadratic through (m, n_m)} at sR = 3/7, same at sR = 5/2}; t = \" <> ToString[tPar], roots3}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Task 4 results — closed-form measures and u-structure on the best site-2 locus b3 = 0 (cells 25-28 and the driver, cells 32-33)\n\n**Chosen locus.** b3 = 0 (gB = -gA gC; 2-dimensional (alpha, gamma), constant cc = 0 t-independent): fewest brackets (13 / 28 per-label), but NOT CG-complete (Task 3). Parametrisation g2 = exp(gamma E23) exp(alpha E12). (For the CG-complete loci the closed forms are the same procedure but with big rational constants; not pursued.)\n\n**Closed forms (cell 25, exact, symbolic in (gA, gC); gauge F_i = 0, F_j = -1, G_j = 0; pivots restricted to monomials in gA, gC so that poles sit only on the excluded set alpha gamma = 0).** Nonzero columns and wedges: **[2,1,0]: 12 columns, 13 wedges; [3,1,0]: 21 columns, 28 wedges** (= the Task 3 counts); symbolic residual of sum of wedges - column = **0 for every column**. The wedges are SPARSE: [3,1,0]: |supp G| = 1 for all but two wedges (a delta function at m = -4 or -3, i.e. a Q-point value; the two exceptions have |supp G| = 2), |supp F| <= 4 (F on 1-4 points); [2,1,0] likewise (|supp G| = 1 except two wedges with |supp G| = 2). **Explicit [2,1,0] formula** (points m = -3,-2,-1,0; the overlap is  sum_{x1} M^(1)_{x1}/M^(1)_vac  sum_{c'} Q^3(theta2 - c' h) sum_wedges Bk2^(2)[F,G], Bk2[F,G] = <Q^3 F>_2<Q^2 G>_2 - <Q^2 F>_2<Q^3 G>_2), per (x1, c'): \n\n- (1|10),1: F = (0,-1,0,0), G = (4092725 gA^2 gC/2516859, 0,0,0); (1|11),0: F = (0,-1,0,0), G = (-6790 gA^2 gC/8649,0,0,0); (1|11),1: F = (0,-1,264 gA/97,0), G = (35 gA gC/9,0,0,0);\n- (2|00),1: F = (0,-1,0,0), G = (2450 gA^2 gC/93217,0,0,0); (2|10),0: F = (0,-1,0,0), G = (-1155 gA^2 gC/961,0,0,0); (2|10),1: F = (0,-1,-2046 gA/97,0), G = (-560 gA gC/25947,0,0,0);\n- (2|20),0: F = (0,-1,-1155 gA/961,0), G = (35 gA gC/27,0,0,0); (2|20),1: F = (0,-1,132 gA/31,0), G = (35 gC/62,0,-121275 gA^2 gC/93217,0); (2|11),0: F = (0,-1,2728 gA/873,0), G = (-3395 gA gC/961,0,0,0); (2|11),1: F = (0,-1,0,0), G = (-280 gA/837,0,0,0);\n- vacuum (2|21),0 (two wedges): F = (-3007 (62 gA - 27 gC)/(297594 gA^2 gC), 0,-1,0), G = (6402 gA gC/961, -5511 gA^2 gC/961, 0,0) and F = (0,0,0,-1), G = (-103499 gA^2 gC/8649,0,0,0); (2|21),1: F = (0,-1,132 gA/31,0), G = (1,0,0,0).\n\n(t = 62/35; the [3,1,0] list of 28 wedges is printed in cell 25; every entry is a Laurent monomial in gA, gC times at most one linear factor.)\n\n**Verification (cell 26).** Overlap identity on ALL states with the closed forms at 3 fresh rational points (gA,gC) = (5/2,-3/7), (-4/3,2/5), (7/3,11/4): max rel dev **< 1e-45.7, 1e-46.0, 1e-45.7 ([2,1,0], 13 wedges)** and **< 1e-44.0, 1e-44.5, 1e-44.5 ([3,1,0], 28 wedges)**; non-vacuity min|lhs|/max|lhs| ~ 1e-6.\n\n**Exponent law (cell 26; gA-free exact).** With gC = sR gA every nonzero entry of every column kernel is A_{mm'} = **gA^(m + m' + k) a_{mm'}(sR, t)** (i.e. gA^((u+u'-2 theta2)/h) x gA^k, the bra-twist exponential in the ladder variable), a_{mm'} polynomial in sR of degree <= 1 (degree 0 in 3 columns), the offset k a single value per column: [2,1,0] k = 8,8,7,8,8,7,7,6,7,6,6,5 for (1|10)1,(1|11)0,(1|11)1,(2|00)1,(2|10)0,(2|10)1,(2|20)0,(2|20)1,(2|11)0,(2|11)1,(2|21)0,(2|21)1; [3,1,0] k from 11 down to 7 (printed in cell 26/33; it drops by 1 per c' and with the label).\n\n**t-dependence — exact closed forms in (sR, t) (cell 33, 15 (h,theta) points, every coefficient fitted as a rational function of t and reproduced exactly at all points; h-independent: depends on t = theta12/h only).** Denominators are products of t, t-1, t+1 ([2,1,0]) and t, t-1, t-2, t+1, t+2 ([3,1,0]) — poles at the ladder-coincidence values; numerators factor into linear factors t+k (k = -6..4) times small integers except a few non-factorising quadratics (6+t+t^2, 3+5t+t^2, t^2+2t-12, t^2-4t-24). E.g. [2,1,0], vacuum column (2|21), c'=1 (rank 2): a_{-3,-2} = 1, a_{-3,-1} = -2(t+2)/t; (2|21), c'=0: a_{-3,-2} = (t+1)/(t-1) - sR (t+1)/t, a_{-3,-1} = 2 sR (t+1)(t+2)/t^2, a_{-3,0} = -sR (t+1)^2 (t+2)/((t-1) t^2), a_{-2,-1} = -sR (t+2)(t+3)/t^2. [3,1,0], vacuum (3|31), c'=1: a_{-4,-3} = 1, a_{-4,-2} = -3(t+3)/t, a_{-4,-1} = 3(t+2)(t+3)/((t-1) t), a_{-3,-2} = 2(t+3)(t+4)/(t(t+1)). The full list for all 12 resp. 21 columns is in the cell-33 output. The numerator factors (t+k) are the values theta1 - x_m = h(t - m) of the ladder-1 pole polynomial at the ladder-2 nodes m = -k, i.e. the cross-ladder structure appears as products of ladder-1 pole factors at the nodes, as predicted, but not as a single \"cross pole x low-degree polynomial\".\n\n**u-form tests (cells 27-28; mirror of the site-1 class tests, cross-ladder poles (t - n - m), n = 0..λ1).** For the rank-2 columns the planes P = Im A satisfy dim(P0 cap class) for (a) wgt_S(m) p(m) on the column support S: 1,2,3 (|S| = 2) or 0,1,2 (|S| = 3) for deg p <= 0,1,2 — the trivial dimension count; for (b) the global SoV measure, (c) bare polynomial, (d) cross-pole classes: **0 for deg <= 1 in [3,1,0]** (0,0,1 at degree 2 for [2,1,0] only by dimension count) — **no column is natural in any of the global classes**. The rank-2 columns with 3-point support are all of the form delta_{-4} ^ (2-point vector): the unique annihilator on S = {-4,-3,-2} is n = (0, 1, r) with r s-independent and t-dependent ([3,1,0], e.g. (2|20),1 at t = 62/35: r = -8342/13527; roots of the quadratic through n_m: -4 and -39567/17698) — NOT of the site-1 form n_m = -m(t+m+1) (roots 0, -(t+1)); one [2,1,0] column, (2|20),1, has irrational roots ((-66607 +- sqrt(1620601801))/31342). Rank-4 columns: [3,1,0] (2|21)1, (3|20)1, (3|30)0, (3|30)1, (3|21)0, (3|31)0, (3|31)1; [2,1,0] (2|21)0: two wedges delta-point ^ 3-4-point vector plus delta ^ delta. **Conclusion: the site-2 analogue of the 5-bracket formula is the sparse 13 / 28-wedge formula above (point values of Q^2, Q^3 at ladder-2 nodes times short brackets) with explicit rational-in-(t, gA, gC) coefficients; the expected \"w1'^(-(u-theta2)/h) x measure x cross pole x polynomial\" u-form exists only in the trivial sense of the exponent law gA^(m+m'+k) — no per-column natural measure was found.**",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 5: the adjoint quadric as a torus image of the vacuum family (exact). For D = diag(d1, d2, d3): e1 rho(g) rho(D) = rho(D)_11 e1 rho(D^-1 g D), and D^-1 g D has Gauss parameters (alpha d2/d1, beta d3/d1, gamma d3/d2); b3 = beta + alpha gamma scales by d3/d1 and alpha^2 by (d2/d1)^2, so the torus with d1 d3/d2^2 = cc maps the vacuum family {b3 = alpha^2} onto {b3 = cc alpha^2}. Checked on the rep (rho(D) = rho_diag[d], weights of the GT basis). *)\nClearAll[torusImage, ccQuadric, rhoD];\nrhoD[d_] := ρdiag[d];\ntorusImage[{a_, b_, g_}, d_] := {a d[[2]]/d[[1]], b d[[3]]/d[[1]], g d[[3]]/d[[2]]};\nccQuadric = (tPar - 3)/(2 (tPar - 2));\nwT5 = {{7/3, -5/7}, {-3/2, 4/5}, {5/3, 7/2}};\ndQ = {1, 4, 16 ccQuadric};     (* d1 d3/d2^2 = cc *)\ndG = {2, 3, 9/2};              (* d1 d3/d2^2 = 1: the unimodular-type torus *)\ndR = {3/2, -5/4, 7/3};         (* generic torus, d1 d3/d2^2 = 7/3 * 3/2 / (25/16) *)\nratioOf[d_] := d[[1]] d[[3]]/d[[2]]^2;\nexactImage[w_, d_] := Module[{pa = gaussParOf[w], lhs, rhs}, lhs = Ωc[w] . Normal[rhoD[d]]; rhs = rhoD[d][[1, 1]] Normal[gaussCov[torusImage[pa, d]]]; Union[Flatten[lhs - rhs]] === {0}];\nonConic[pa_, cc_] := (pa[[2]] + pa[[1]] pa[[3]] - cc pa[[1]]^2) === 0;\nimgPar[w_, d_] := torusImage[gaussParOf[w], d];\ntab5 = Table[{w, exactImage[w, dQ], onConic[imgPar[w, dQ], ccQuadric], exactImage[w, dG], onConic[imgPar[w, dG], 1], onConic[imgPar[w, dR], ratioOf[dR]]}, {w, wT5}];\n(* converse: any rational point of the quadric b3 = cc alpha^2 is the image of a vacuum-family point under the one-parameter torus (1, 1, cc): (alpha, beta, gamma) -> (alpha, cc beta, cc gamma) *)\nquadPts = {{4, 5}, {4, 3}, {-3, 2}};   (* (alpha, gamma) *)\nconvQ = Table[Module[{a = pp[[1]], g = pp[[2]], b}, b = ccQuadric a^2 - a g; (* point on the quadric; preimage on the vacuum family *) With[{pre = {a, b/ccQuadric, g/ccQuadric}}, {onConic[pre, 1], Union[Flatten[Ωc[{1/a, 1/(g/ccQuadric - a)}] . Normal[rhoD[{1, 1, ccQuadric}]] - rhoD[{1, 1, ccQuadric}][[1, 1]] Normal[gaussCov[{a, b, g}]]]] === {0}}]], {pp, quadPts}];\n(* (i) the section-5 product point of Two-rotations-det-overlap: v1 = Omega_(w1,ystar) rho((w2 - G(z)^T)^-1) = Omega_(w2,ystar) rho((w1 - G(z)^T)^-1), ystar = w2 (t-1)/(t-2), companion frame; first row of the 3x3 product *)\nGz = Gc[zN];\nRw[w_] := Inverse[w IdentityMatrix[3] - Transpose[Gz]];\nystar[w_] := w[[2]] (tPar - 1)/(tPar - 2);\nv1Row[w_] := With[{b = (Pp3[w[[1]], ystar[w]] . Rw[w[[2]]])[[1]]}, b/b[[1]]];\nv1RowB[w_] := With[{b = (Pp3[w[[2]], ystar[w]] . Rw[w[[1]]])[[1]]}, b/b[[1]]];\nccOfRow[b_] := b[[3]]/b[[2]]^2;\ntabV1 = Table[{w, v1Row[w] === v1RowB[w], v1Row[w], ccOfRow[v1Row[w]], N[ccOfRow[v1Row[w]], 6]}, {w, wT5}];\n(* in the diagonal frame the resolvent torus is D = diag(1/(y - z_k)): d1 d3/d2^2 = (y - z2)^2/((y - z1)(y - z3)); is it equal to the quadric constant cc(t) for some y? *)\nySol = Solve[(yy - zN[[2]])^2 2 (tPar - 2) == (tPar - 3) (yy - zN[[1]]) (yy - zN[[3]]), yy];\nratioRes = {N[ySol, 8], Simplify[((yy - zN[[2]])^2/((yy - zN[[1]]) (yy - zN[[3]])) /. ySol)]};\n(* the section-5 ystar values for the sample w: does the diagonal-frame resolvent ratio at y = w2, y*, w1 equal cc(t)? *)\nratAt = Table[{w, Table[(yv - zN[[2]])^2/((yv - zN[[1]]) (yv - zN[[3]])), {yv, {w[[1]], w[[2]], ystar[w]}}]}, {w, wT5}];\nGrid[{{\"t, quadric constant cc(t) = (t-3)/(2(t-2)); d for the quadric torus (d1 d3/d2^2 = cc)\", {tPar, ccQuadric, dQ}}, {\"{w, Omega_c[w] rho(D) = rho(D)_11 e1 rho(g') exactly, g' on b3 = cc alpha^2; same for the unimodular torus d = (2,3,9/2) -> b3 = alpha^2; generic torus -> constant d1d3/d2^2}\", tab5}, {\"converse: {preimage on the vacuum family (cc=1), image equality}, 3 quadric points\", convQ}, {\"section-5 product point v1 (companion frame): {w, two descriptions agree (first row), normalised first row (1, a, b3), b1 b3/b2^2 exact, numeric}\", tabV1}, {\"torus ratio y-solutions of (y-z2)^2/((y-z1)(y-z3)) = cc(t)\", ratioRes}, {\"diagonal-frame resolvent ratio (y-z2)^2/((y-z1)(y-z3)) at y = w1, w2, ystar\", ratAt}, {\"torus statement: cc = d1 d3/d2^2 (adjoint: cc = (t-3)/(2(t-2)) = (3/4) kappa_singlet with kappa_singlet = 2(t-3)/(3(t-2)))\", {ccQuadric, 3/4 2 (tPar - 3)/(3 (tPar - 2))}}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Task 5 results — the adjoint quadric as a torus image of the vacuum family (cell 30; exact, rep-generic, identical for both reps)\n\nAnalytic fact (spec): e1 rho(g) rho(D) = rho(D)_11 e1 rho(D^-1 g D) and D^-1 g D has Gauss parameters (alpha d2/d1, beta d3/d1, gamma d3/d2), so b3 = beta + alpha gamma scales by d3/d1 and alpha^2 by (d2/d1)^2: **the torus with d1 d3/d2^2 = cc maps the vacuum family {b3 = alpha^2} onto {b3 = cc alpha^2}**. Verified on the rep (rho(D) = `ρdiag[d]`, GT weight basis), t = 62/35, cc(t) = (t-3)/(2(t-2)) = 43/16:\n\n| check | result |\n|---|---|\n| `Ωc[w]`.rho(D) = rho(D)_11 e1 rho(g') EXACTLY, with g' = (alpha d2/d1, beta d3/d1, gamma d3/d2), for d = (1, 4, 43) (d1 d3/d2^2 = 43/16), at 3 rational w | True x 3; and g' lies on the quadric b3 = (43/16) alpha^2 (exact): True x 3 |\n| same for the unimodular-type torus d = (2, 3, 9/2) (d1 d3 = d2^2): image on the vacuum family b3 = alpha^2 | True x 3, True x 3 |\n| generic torus d = (3/2, -5/4, 7/3): image on b3 = (d1 d3/d2^2) alpha^2 | True x 3 |\n| converse: any rational point (alpha, gamma) of the quadric is the image of a vacuum-family point under the one-parameter torus d = (1, 1, cc): (alpha, beta, gamma) -> (alpha, cc beta, cc gamma); exact equality of covectors | True x 3 |\n\n**So the adjoint quadric is {Ωc[w]·rho(D) : D = diag(d1,d2,d3), d1 d3/d2^2 = (t-3)/(2(t-2))}** and the [3,1,0] best locus (cc = 1) is the vacuum family modulo the unimodular-type torus d1 d3 = d2^2. With the relation cc = (3/4) kappa_singlet, kappa_singlet = 2(t-3)/(3(t-2)), noted: d1 d3/d2^2 = (3/4) kappa (exact check 43/16 = 43/16 at t = 62/35).\n\n**(i) Comparison with the section-5 product point of `Two-rotations-det-overlap.md`** (v1 = Ω_{(w1,ystar)} rho((w2 - G(z)^T)^-1) = Ω_{(w2,ystar)} rho((w1 - G(z)^T)^-1), ystar = w2 (t-1)/(t-2), companion frame; z = (3/2,5/4,2/3)): the two descriptions of v1 have the same first row (True at 3 sample w). The resolvent is the torus diag(1/(y - z_k)) in the DIAGONAL frame, a non-GT-diagonal matrix in the companion frame, so the companion-frame torus statement above does not apply to it directly. Direct computation of the first row of v1 = (1, a, b3): b1 b3/b2^2 = 1925073/1282288 = 1.5013 at w = (7/3,-5/7); 781337/766322 = 1.0196 at (-3/2,4/5); 15023/15125 = 0.9933 at (5/3,7/2) — a symmetric rational function of (w1,w2) (setting it equal to 43/16 is a polynomial equation of degree 4 in w2 for given w1, i.e. an algebraic curve), NOT constant: **the section-5 site-1 factor lies on the adjoint quadric only along a curve in the (w1,w2) plane, and is not on the vacuum family (value 1) either**. The diagonal-frame resolvent ratio (y - z2)^2/((y - z1)(y - z3)) equals cc(t) = 43/16 at y = 0.43438 and y = 1.53476 (two real roots, z = (3/2,5/4,2/3)); at y = w1, w2, ystar of the samples it is 0.845, 1.262, 0.848 / 1.163, -2.170, 1.103 / 1.042, 0.893, 1.027 — none equals 43/16. **Relation: no identification; the quadric constant is reproduced by a diagonal-frame resolvent only at two special values of y that are not the section-5 values (not forced).** (ii) cc = (3/4) kappa_singlet becomes d1 d3/d2^2 = (3/4) kappa: noted, nothing more.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Task 3/4 DRIVER: z-independence of the K maps and the (h, theta)-dependence of the site-2 data (conic constants, the b3 = 0 locus, bracket counts, the column kernels on b3 = 0). RUN LAST: this cell wipes Global`* (it re-runs the setup cells with other parameter lines, read from this notebook's own file); all data live in the context Dr`. Afterwards re-run the cells above to restore the base state of the chosen rep. Each point is under a 200 s guard. *)\nDr`nbFile = \"C:/Users/pryan/git-projects/gaudin-cg/Paul/Mathematica/new-conventions/L2-site2-rotation-brackets.wb\";\nDr`tmp = StringReplace[Dr`nbFile, \".wb\" -> \"-driver-tmp.wl\"];\nDr`codeCells := Dr`codeCells = Select[Import[Dr`nbFile, \"RawJSON\"][\"cells\"], #[\"kind\"] == 2 &][[All, \"value\"]];\nDr`pick[s_String] := First[Select[Dr`codeCells, StringContainsQ[#, s] &]];\nDr`seq = {\"the ONLY rep switch\", \"eigenstates of the twisted chain\", \"dual Q's: Q^j(x)\", \"physical-space Gauss factors\", \"untwisted L=2 B(u)\", \"Task 1: SoV wavefunction rule\", \"Site-1 regression (general notebook Task 2)\", \"Site-1 regression (general notebook Task 3)\", \"Task 1: the mirror.\", \"Task 2: ladder-2 column tensors per site-1 label\", \"Task 3a: loci in g2\"};\nDr`ev[txt_String] := (Export[Dr`tmp, txt, \"Text\", CharacterEncoding -> \"UTF-8\"]; Get[Dr`tmp, CharacterEncoding -> \"UTF-8\"]);\nDr`lamStr = ToString[Λ, InputForm];\n(* NB: no Module locals here: the first setup cell wipes Global` and with it every Module variable *)\nDr`run[hs_String, ths_String, zs_String] := (Dr`t0 = AbsoluteTime[];\n  Dr`subs = {\"Λ = {2, 1, 0};\" -> \"Λ = \" <> Dr`lamStr <> \";\", \"hN = 1/2; thN = {2/7, -3/5}; zN = {3/2, 5/4, 2/3};\" -> \"hN = \" <> hs <> \"; thN = \" <> ths <> \"; zN = \" <> zs <> \";\"};\n  Scan[Dr`ev[StringReplace[Dr`pick[#], Dr`subs]] &, Dr`seq];\n  <|\"t\" -> ToExpression[\"tPar\"], \"Kh\" -> ToExpression[\"Kh\"], \"conic\" -> ToExpression[\"conicTab2\"],\n    \"cntGen\" -> ToExpression[\"Total[Flatten[rankTab2[tens2[Normal[gaussCov[{2/3, -3/7, 5/4}]]]]]]/2\"],\n    \"cntB0\" -> ToExpression[\"Total[Flatten[rankTab2[tens2[Normal[gaussCov[{1, -2, 2}]]]]]]/2\"],\n    \"cntVac\" -> ToExpression[\"Total[Flatten[rankTab2[tens2[Normal[gaussCov[{3, 3, 2}]]]]]]/2\"],\n    \"mats\" -> ToExpression[\"Association[Table[k -> amat[Expand /@ (colS2 @@ k /. gB -> -gA gC)], {k, colKeys}]]\"],\n    \"colKeys\" -> ToExpression[\"colKeys\"], \"labels\" -> ToExpression[\"labRule\"], \"pts\" -> ToExpression[\"mPts\"], \"supp\" -> ToExpression[\"Length[supp2]\"],\n    \"time\" -> AbsoluteTime[] - Dr`t0|>);\n(* parameter points: (h, theta, z); the first is the base point of the notebook *)\nDr`pts = {{\"base\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, -3/5}\", \"{3/2, 5/4, 2/3}\"}, {\"z' = (3/2,5/4,3/7)\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, -3/5}\", \"{3/2, 5/4, 3/7}\"}, {\"z'' = (2,5/4,2/3)\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, -3/5}\", \"{2, 5/4, 2/3}\"},\n  {\"h=1/3, th=(1/5,-4/9)\", \"1/3\", \"{1/5, -4/9}\", \"{3/2, 5/4, 2/3}\"}, {\"h=1/2, th=(3/7,-1/4)\", \"1/2\", \"{3/7, -1/4}\", \"{3/2, 5/4, 2/3}\"}, {\"th2=1/5\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, 1/5}\", \"{3/2, 5/4, 2/3}\"}, {\"th2=-26/105\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, -26/105}\", \"{3/2, 5/4, 2/3}\"},\n  {\"th2=-27/28\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, -27/28}\", \"{3/2, 5/4, 2/3}\"}, {\"th2=-37/42\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, -37/42}\", \"{3/2, 5/4, 2/3}\"}, {\"th2=-1/70\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, -1/70}\", \"{3/2, 5/4, 2/3}\"}, {\"th2=-3/7\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, -3/7}\", \"{3/2, 5/4, 2/3}\"},\n  {\"th2=-5/3\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, -5/3}\", \"{3/2, 5/4, 2/3}\"}, {\"th2=1/3\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, 1/3}\", \"{3/2, 5/4, 2/3}\"},\n  {\"th2=2/5\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, 2/5}\", \"{3/2, 5/4, 2/3}\"}, {\"th2=-4/5\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, -4/5}\", \"{3/2, 5/4, 2/3}\"}, {\"th2=-2/3\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, -2/3}\", \"{3/2, 5/4, 2/3}\"}, {\"th2=-6/5\", \"1/2\", \"{2/7, -6/5}\", \"{3/2, 5/4, 2/3}\"}};\nDr`runSafe[i_] := With[{r = TimeConstrained[AbsoluteTiming[Dr`run[Dr`pts[[i, 2]], Dr`pts[[i, 3]], Dr`pts[[i, 4]]]], 200, $Failed]}, If[r === $Failed, Nothing, Dr`pts[[i, 1]] -> r[[2]]]];\n{Dr`tAll, Dr`res} = AbsoluteTiming[Association[Table[Dr`runSafe[i], {i, Length[Dr`pts]}]]];\nDr`KhBase = Dr`res[\"base\"][\"Kh\"];\nDr`zTest = Table[{k, Dr`res[k][\"Kh\"] === Dr`KhBase}, {k, {\"z' = (3/2,5/4,3/7)\", \"z'' = (2,5/4,2/3)\"}}];\nGrid[Join[{{\"point\", \"t = theta12/h\", \"K maps identical to the base ones (z-test points only, exact)\", \"# support states\", \"per-label count: generic / b3 = 0 point / vacuum-family point\", \"time (s)\"}}, Table[{k, Dr`res[k][\"t\"], If[StringStartsQ[k, \"z\"], Dr`res[k][\"Kh\"] === Dr`KhBase, \"-\"], Dr`res[k][\"supp\"], {Dr`res[k][\"cntGen\"], Dr`res[k][\"cntB0\"], Dr`res[k][\"cntVac\"]}, N[Dr`res[k][\"time\"], 3]}, {k, Keys[Dr`res]}], {{\"total (s)\", Dr`tAll, \"\", \"\", \"\", \"\"}}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* Analysis of the driver data (only the context Dr` is used; run right after the driver). (1) z-independence and the persistence of the b3 = 0 locus and of the counts across (h, theta); (2) the t-dependence of the conic constants cc of the Pfaffian factors gB + gA gC = cc gA^2 (rational functions of t from the sample points; the Moebius ansatz cc = (p t + q)/(r t + s)); (3) the column kernels A_{mm'} = gA^(m + m' + k) a_{mm'}(sR, t) on b3 = 0, with sR = gC/gA, each coefficient fitted as a rational function of t through all sample points (exact, over-determined). *)\nClearAll[tv, sR, gA, gC];\nDr`hts = Select[Keys[Dr`res], Not[StringStartsQ[#, \"z\"]] &];\nDr`ts = Table[Dr`res[k][\"t\"], {k, Dr`hts}];\nDr`ratFit[ts_, vals_] := Module[{res = {}, ns},\n  If[AllTrue[vals, # === 0 &], Return[0]];\n  Do[If[res === {} && m + n + 2 <= Length[ts] - 1,\n    ns = NullSpace[Table[Join[Table[ts[[i]]^k, {k, 0, m}], Table[-vals[[i]] ts[[i]]^k, {k, 0, n}]], {i, Length[ts]}]];\n    If[Length[ns] == 1, res = Factor[(Sum[ns[[1, k + 1]] tv^k, {k, 0, m}])/(Sum[ns[[1, m + 2 + k]] tv^k, {k, 0, n}])]]], {tot, 0, 12}, {m, 0, tot}, {n, 0, tot - m}];\n  If[res === {}, $Failed, res]];\n(* (1) *)\nDr`persist = Table[{k, Dr`res[k][\"t\"], Dr`res[k][\"supp\"], Dr`res[k][\"cntGen\"], Dr`res[k][\"cntB0\"], Dr`res[k][\"cntVac\"], Length[Dr`res[k][\"conic\"]]}, {k, Dr`hts}];\n(* (2) conic constants grouped by (label, c'). A group with one conic is fitted directly; with n > 1 conics the values at each t are an unordered set, so candidate rational functions of type (d, d) are interpolated through one value per point at the first 2d+1 points (n^(2d+1) choices) and kept if the prediction lies in the set of values at every other point *)\nDr`ccGroups = Association[Table[g -> Table[Sort[Cases[Dr`res[k][\"conic\"], {g[[1]], g[[2]], _, c_} :> c]], {k, Dr`hts}], {g, DeleteDuplicates[{#[[1]], #[[2]]} & /@ Dr`res[\"base\"][\"conic\"]]}]];\nDr`fitD[ts_, vals_, d_] := Module[{ns = NullSpace[Table[Join[Table[ts[[i]]^k, {k, 0, d}], Table[-vals[[i]] ts[[i]]^k, {k, 0, d}]], {i, Length[ts]}]]}, If[Length[ns] == 1, Factor[(Sum[ns[[1, k + 1]] tv^k, {k, 0, d}])/(Sum[ns[[1, d + 2 + k]] tv^k, {k, 0, d}])], $Failed]];\nDr`searchCC[lists_] := Module[{n = Length[lists[[1]]], out = {}},\n  Do[If[Length[out] < n && Length[lists] > 2 d + 2,\n    With[{k = 2 d + 1}, out = DeleteDuplicates[Select[Table[Dr`fitD[Dr`ts[[;; k]], Table[lists[[i, ch[[i]]]], {i, k}], d], {ch, Tuples[Range[n], k]}], # =!= $Failed && And @@ Table[MemberQ[lists[[i]], # /. tv -> Dr`ts[[i]]], {i, k + 1, Length[lists]}] &]]]], {d, 1, 3}];\n  out];\nDr`ccFits = Association[KeyValueMap[Function[{g, lists}, g -> If[Length[Union[Length /@ lists]] != 1, \"number of conics changes with t\", If[Length[lists[[1]]] == 1, {Dr`ratFit[Dr`ts, lists[[All, 1]]]}, Dr`searchCC[lists]]]], Dr`ccGroups]];\nDr`ccCheck = Association[KeyValueMap[Function[{g, fits}, g -> If[ListQ[fits] && FreeQ[fits, $Failed], And @@ Table[MemberQ[Dr`ccGroups[g][[i]], f /. tv -> Dr`ts[[i]]], {f, fits}, {i, Length[Dr`ts]}], \"-\"]], Dr`ccFits]];\n(* t -> tp shifts: is a fitted conic constant cc2(t) equal to the site-1 adjoint formula cc1(tp) = (tp - 3)/(2 (tp - 2)) with tp = t + k or tp = k - t (k = -6..6)? *)\nDr`cc1[x_] := (x - 3)/(2 (x - 2));\nDr`shiftMatch = Association[KeyValueMap[Function[{g, fits}, g -> If[ListQ[fits] && FreeQ[fits, $Failed], Table[Flatten[Table[Join[If[Simplify[f - Dr`cc1[tv + kk]] === 0, {\"tp = t + \" <> ToString[kk]}, {}], If[Simplify[f - Dr`cc1[kk - tv]] === 0, {\"tp = \" <> ToString[kk] <> \" - t\"}, {}]], {kk, -6, 6}]], {f, fits}], \"-\"]], Dr`ccFits]];\nDr`ccAtT = Association[KeyValueMap[Function[{g, lists}, g -> Table[{Dr`ts[[i]], lists[[i]]}, {i, {1, 2}}]], Dr`ccGroups]];\n(* (3) kernels *)\nDr`bk = Dr`res[\"base\"]; Dr`pp = Dr`bk[\"pts\"]; Dr`np = Length[Dr`pp];\nDr`nzK = Select[Dr`bk[\"colKeys\"], Not[AllTrue[Flatten[Dr`bk[\"mats\"][#]], # === 0 &]] &];\nDr`ent[k_, key_, i_, j_] := Together[Dr`res[k][\"mats\"][key][[i, j]] /. gC -> sR gA];\nDr`kOff[key_] := Union[Flatten[Table[With[{e = Factor[Dr`ent[\"base\", key, i, j]]}, If[e === 0, Nothing, Exponent[Numerator[e], gA, Min] - Exponent[Denominator[e], gA, Min] - Dr`pp[[i]] - Dr`pp[[j]]]], {i, Dr`np}, {j, i + 1, Dr`np}]]];\nDr`kern[k_, key_, i_, j_] := Together[Dr`ent[k, key, i, j]/gA^(Dr`pp[[i]] + Dr`pp[[j]] + First[Dr`kOff[key]])];\nDr`sDeg[key_] := Max[Flatten[Table[Exponent[Numerator[Dr`kern[\"base\", key, i, j]], sR], {i, Dr`np}, {j, i + 1, Dr`np}]]];\nDr`kernFit[key_] := Module[{dg = Dr`sDeg[key]}, Association[Flatten[Table[{Dr`pp[[i]], Dr`pp[[j]]} -> Sum[sR^q Dr`ratFit[Dr`ts, Table[Coefficient[Numerator[Dr`kern[k, key, i, j]], sR, q]/Denominator[Dr`kern[k, key, i, j]], {k, Dr`hts}]], {q, 0, dg}], {i, Dr`np}, {j, i + 1, Dr`np}]]]];\n{Dr`tKern, Dr`kernFits} = AbsoluteTiming[Association[Table[key -> Dr`kernFit[key], {key, Dr`nzK}]]];\nDr`kernOK = Association[Table[key -> And @@ Flatten[Table[Together[(Dr`kernFits[key][{Dr`pp[[i]], Dr`pp[[j]]}] /. tv -> Dr`res[k][\"t\"]) - Dr`kern[k, key, i, j]] === 0, {k, Dr`hts}, {i, Dr`np}, {j, i + 1, Dr`np}]], {key, Dr`nzK}]];\nDr`kernList = Association[Table[key -> Select[Normal[Dr`kernFits[key]], #[[2]] =!= 0 &], {key, Dr`nzK}]];\nDr`poles = Union[Flatten[Cases[Factor[Denominator[Together[#]]] & /@ Flatten[Values /@ Values[Dr`kernFits]], tv + c_. | tv - c_. | tv, {0, Infinity}]]];\nDr`polesT = Union[Flatten[FactorList[Denominator[Together[#]]][[All, 1]] & /@ Select[Flatten[Values /@ Values[Dr`kernFits]], # =!= 0 &]]];\nGrid[{{\"(1) per sample point: {name, t, # support states, per-label count generic / b3 = 0 point / vacuum point, # conic factors}\", Dr`persist}, {\"z-independence (K maps exactly equal at z' and z'')\", Dr`zTest}, {\"(2) conic constants: sorted values fitted as rational functions of t, per (label, c')\", Normal[Dr`ccFits]}, {\"fits reproduce the sampled values exactly\", Normal[Dr`ccCheck]}, {\"conic constants at the first two sample points t = 62/35 and t = 29/15: (label, c-prime) -> {{t, values}, ...}\", Normal[Dr`ccAtT]}, {\"matches with the site-1 adjoint formula cc1(tp) = (tp - 3)/(2(tp - 2)) at tp = t + k or k - t (k = -6..6): per conic\", Normal[Dr`shiftMatch]}, {\"(3) kernels: # columns, all fits exact at every point?, time (s)\", {Length[Dr`nzK], And @@ Values[Dr`kernOK], Dr`tKern}}, {\"gA offsets k per column\", Table[{Dr`bk[\"labels\"][[key[[1]]]], key[[2]], Dr`kOff[key]}, {key, Dr`nzK}]}, {\"distinct irreducible denominator factors of all fitted kernel coefficients\", Dr`polesT}, {\"kernel coefficients a_{mm'}(sR, t) per column: {labelIdx, c'} -> {{m, m'} -> expression}\", Normal[Dr`kernList]}}, Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### Driver results (cells 32-33; the driver wipes Global`, run last)\n\nPoints: base (h = 1/2, theta = (2/7,-3/5), z = (3/2,5/4,2/3)), z' = (3/2,5/4,3/7), z'' = (2,5/4,2/3) (same h, theta), and the (h, theta) points h = 1/3 theta = (1/5,-4/9) [t = 29/15]; h = 1/2 theta = (3/7,-1/4) [19/14]; theta2 = 1/5, -26/105, -27/28, -37/42, -1/70, -3/7, -5/3, 1/3, 2/5, -4/5, -2/3, -6/5 (h = 1/2) [t = 6/35, 16/15, 5/2, 7/3, 3/5, 10/7, 82/21, -2/21, -8/35, 76/35, 40/21, 104/35]: 15 values of t in all, base included (the last four points were added after a first run with 11 points showed that one [3,1,0] kernel coefficient needs numerator degree 4 over a degree-5 denominator, which 11 points cannot over-determine; the rational fit loop was also extended to total degree 12). No point stalled (guard 200 s per point).\n\n| result | [2,1,0] | [3,1,0] |\n|---|---|---|\n| **K maps identical (exact rationals) at z' and z''** | **True, True** | **True, True** |\n| support size (# SoV states) at every point | 35 | 103 |\n| per-label counts at every point: generic / b3 = 0 point / vacuum-family point | 17 / 13 / 17 | 40 / 28 / 40 |\n| # conic factors at every point | 1 | 5 |\n| conic constants as exact rational functions of t (reproduce all 15 sampled values) | (2\\|21)0: **(t+2)/(2(t+1))** (66/97 at t = 62/35, 59/88 at 29/15) | (2\\|21)0: (2t^2+5t-4)/(2(t-1)(t+2)); (3\\|30)0: (t-1)(8t^2+13t-7)/(6(t-2) t (t+1)); (3\\|31)0: (t^2+3t+6)/(3t(t+1)), (t+2)/(2t), 2(t+3)/(3(t+1)) |\n| site-1 adjoint formula cc1(t') = (t'-3)/(2(t'-2)) matched at t' = t + k or k - t (k = -6..6) | only t' = 1 - t for the (2\\|21)0 conic | none |\n| kernels A = gA^(m+m'+k) a_{mm'}(sR,t) on b3 = 0: # columns; all coefficient fits exact at all points | 12; True | 21; True |\n| denominator factors of the fitted coefficients | t, t-1, t+1 | t-2, t-1, t, t+1, t+2 |\n| time (s): driver; analysis | 38.7; 1.3 | 357; 5.7 |",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
