  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "### site-2 rotation brackets (Stage A) — result (2026-10-11)\n\n**Setting.** gl(3), L = 2, companion frame, h = 1/2, theta = (2/7,-3/5) (t = 62/35), z = (3/2,5/4,2/3); [2,1,0] (64 states) and [3,1,0] (225 states); everything exact except the eigenstates/Q's (prec 60, all identities 1e-40 or better). Notebook state: the cells were not executed natively by VS Code (file opened with the `code` CLI; `wolfbook_runCell` answers \"NOT executed\", the controller is not associated); every code cell was evaluated in the shared kernel K1 from exactly its saved source text and the printed results are in the markdown cells; the driver (cell 32) re-reads this file and wipes Global`.\n\n**1. Vacuum-family identification (cells 13-14; exact).** `Ωc[w]` = e1 exp(E12/w1) exp(-E13/(w1 w2)) exp((w1+w2)/(w1 w2) E23) equals the Gauss rotation (alpha, beta, gamma) = (1/w1, -1/(w1 w2), (w1+w2)/(w1 w2)) exactly (3 rational w); first row (1, 1/w1, 1/w1^2), so b3 = alpha^2 (symbolic); converse: rational points of beta = alpha^2 - alpha gamma equal `Ωc[{1/alpha, 1/(gamma-alpha)}]` exactly (6 points); `Ωc[w]`(x)`Ωc[w]` is an exact left eigen-covector of t_1, t_2, t_3 with the companion-matrix twist G(w1,w2,w3) (any w3; control G^T fails). The [3,1,0] closed-form lambda2-group measures read w1^(-(u-theta1)/h) x SoV measure x 1/(u-theta2+h) x polynomial, amplitudes 48 (t-3)(t+1)/(t w1^8) and -12 (t-3)(w2+3 w1)/(w2 w1^9), and the end-point exception omega(theta1-h) = 3(s-1)/(3s-2) = **3 w1/(w2 + 3 w1)** (verified exactly against the tensors and on all 225 states, 1e-43.7..1e-46.3).\n\n**2. Site-1 support rule for site-2 rotations (cell 16-17): NOT (lambda1|lambda1 c1).** e1 (x) e_nu involves ALL dim V site-1 labels on a triangular set of pairs: 35 of 64 ([2,1,0]) and 103 of 225 ([3,1,0]) SoV states; only 15 resp. 29 of them have x1 = (lambda1|lambda1 c1). The factors M^(1)_{x1}/M^(1)_vac are single Q^3 ratios only for that family; in general they carry ladder-1 2x2 minors. No additive weight rule (SoV covectors are not weight eigen-covectors). K maps: ranks per site-1 label {1,2,4,2,4,6,4,8} ([2,1,0]) and {1,2,4,2,4,6,5,9,2,5,9,12,4,9,15} ([3,1,0]), per site-2 label {1,2,3,2,4,6,4,8} / {1,2,3,2,4,6,4,8,2,5,8,12,4,9,15}; rationalisation error 6e-78 / 2.7e-76, denominators <= 7 / 11 digits; **z-independence exact** (K identical at z' and z''), overlap identity via K 1e-41..1e-46.\n\n**3. Tensors and counts (cell 19).** Column supports <= 4 / 5 points (rank <= 4 automatic). **Per-label automatic count 17 ([2,1,0]) and 40 ([3,1,0])** against the site-1 numbers **5 / 7** (generic) and 4 / 5 (reduced); block form (ladder-1 minors absorbed): matrix ranks 11 / 22 (generic), 15 / 35 products. Bracket and overlap identities 1e-41..1e-47.\n\n**4. Loci (cells 21-22 and driver).** [2,1,0]: two non-automatic columns, loci b3 = 0 (cc = 0; (gB+gA gC)^2) and the conic b3 = cc alpha^2 with **cc(t) = (t+2)/(2(t+1)) = cc1(1-t)** (66/97 at t = 62/35; 59/88 at 29/15); joint genuine locus empty. [3,1,0]: 11 non-automatic columns; conic constants (t-laws): (2t^2+5t-4)/(2(t-1)(t+2)), (t-1)(8t^2+13t-7)/(6(t-2) t (t+1)), (t^2+3t+6)/(3t(t+1)), (t+2)/(2t), 2(t+3)/(3(t+1)) (values 2273/1188, -453483/96224, 8852/9021, 33/31, 334/291 at t = 62/35); genuine part empty for the single 5-point columns ((3|30),0) and (vacuum,0); 25 maximal column sets (24 pairs -> curves, one 4-set -> b3 = 0). **The best locus is NOT the vacuum family**: on beta + alpha gamma = alpha^2 (the Omega_c family) the count equals the generic one (17 / 40) and cc = 1 occurs nowhere; Ωc[w] does not lie on any reducing locus. Cheapest locus: b3 = 0 (**13 / 28**; block {10,12} / {15,23}); cheapest CG-complete: conic 66 alpha^2 = 97 b3 (**16**, [2,1,0]) and dim-1 curves (**38**, [3,1,0]).\n\n**5. Reach (cell 23; exact).** Undo identity exact on all HW kets (6 resp. 10 HW states): True. Generic / vacuum family / quadric / conic / curves: all weights (7 of 7; 12 of 12), rank 2 on every double weight (CG-complete); **b3 = 0: 5 of 7 / 7 of 12 weights (ranks 1 on (1,1,1); 0,1,1 on the [3,1,0] double weights): NOT complete**.\n\n**6. Closed forms and u-form (cells 25-28, 33).** On b3 = 0: 12 / 21 columns, **13 / 28 wedges**, exact symbolic decomposition (residual 0), verified on all states at three fresh points (1e-45.7 / 1e-44.0); wedges sparse (|supp G| = 1 except two, |supp F| <= 4); explicit [2,1,0] formula printed in cell 29; exponent law A_{mm'} = gA^(m+m'+k) a_{mm'}(sR, t), a affine in sR; **a_{mm'}(sR,t) exact rational functions of t** (15 (h,theta) points; poles t in {0,1,-1} resp. {0,1,2,-1,-2}); no column is natural in the global SoV-measure / polynomial / cross-pole classes (d <= 1); rank-2 3-point columns are delta ^ (2-point vector) with t-dependent ratio. The expected w'^(-(u-theta2)/h) x measure x cross pole x polynomial u-form holds only as the exponent law.\n\n**7. Torus statement (cell 30; exact).** The adjoint quadric is {Ωc[w] rho(D): d1 d3/d2^2 = (t-3)/(2(t-2))} (exact on the rep, 3 w, d = (1,4,43), converse with d = (1,1,cc)); the unimodular-type torus d1 d3 = d2^2 preserves the vacuum family. The section-5 product point's site-1 factor has b1 b3/b2^2 = 1.5013, 1.0196, 0.9933 at three w (a non-constant symmetric function of (w1,w2); on the quadric only along a curve); the diagonal-frame resolvent ratio (y-z2)^2/((y-z1)(y-z3)) equals cc(t) at y = 0.43438, 1.53476 only; cc = (3/4) kappa_singlet becomes d1 d3/d2^2 = (3/4) kappa.\n\n**8. Timings.** [2,1,0]: cells 2-30 total 6 s, driver 39 s (15 points) + analysis 1.3 s. [3,1,0]: main cells 75 s (of which the subset scan 40 s), driver 357 s + analysis 5.7 s; [3,2,0] (cell 35): main cells 58 s, driver 431 s. All three reps well under 10 min.\n\n**8b. [3,2,0] (cell 35).** Same picture: support 122 of 225 (41 in the (lambda1|lambda1 c1) family), z-independent; per-label count 54 vs the site-1 11 / 9; vacuum-family and quadric points give no reduction; b3 = 0 gives 43 but is not CG-complete (9 of 12 weights); the vacuum-x1 conic constants are 2(t+2)/(3(t+1)) and (t+2)/(2(t+1)) = cc1(1-t) (same as the adjoint).\n\n**9. Surprises.** (i) The mirror is NOT cheap: the SoV construction is strongly site-asymmetric — a rotation on site 1 with the vacuum on site 2 needs one Q-ratio on ladder 2 (5 / 7 brackets), a rotation on site 2 with the vacuum on site 1 involves every ladder-1 monomial (17 / 40 brackets per-label). (ii) The vacuum family is not special on site 2; the cheap locus b3 = 0 is not CG-complete; the CG-complete loci reduce the count only by 1-2. (iii) cc2(t) = cc1(1-t) for the adjoint is a clean t -> 1 - t shift (not t -> -t). (iv) The SoV covectors are not weight-graded (naive weight rule fails).\n\n**10. What this means for Stage B (two-site K tensor).** The two one-site supports are NOT both \"vacuum on the other site + one Q-ratio\": that structure holds for the site-1 rotation (support (lambda1|lambda1 c2) on site 2) but not for the site-2 rotation (triangular support, all site-1 labels, 35/103 SoV pairs). The (c, c') block decomposition of plan section 1 is nevertheless well defined, since every SoV label maps to (ladder minor, lone point) on each ladder and the blocks A^(c1,c') of the nu1 = 1 slice are exactly the matrices of cell 19 (ranks 3,3,3,2 / 6,6,6,4); the nu2 = 1 slice reproduces the site-1 K maps and the nu1 = 1 slice is cell 16 (both slices of the same 225 x 225 expansion). Expect the general (nu1, nu2) support to be at least the union of the triangular and the vacuum-family pattern, with block ranks of order 10 per (c1, c') for generic pairs; the two slices already have different counts (5 / 7 for the site-1 rotation vs 17 / 40 for the site-2 rotation), so no site-symmetric product structure of the \"decoupling\" test of plan section 6 can be expected. Suggested Stage B order: build the 225 x 225 K once (cell 16 is the template; one linear solve per covector, 3 s), then compute block ranks for g1 x g2 at generic points and on the vacuum families before any locus work.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  }
 ],
 "metadata": {}
}